/* 段落记忆 · 词层 2 · 子块 d：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(2,{"sub":"d","par":{"search":{"tw":[["look",0],["hunt",3],["web",6],["research",0],["investigate",2],["examine",2],["feel",3],["fish",3]],"en":"My grandmother lost her keys on the beach. We started a search right after breakfast. She began to look under every bench, and I went to hunt along the water. My uncle used the web to research the lost and found office, then called the police, who promised to investigate. A fisherman helped us examine the wet sand near the boats. We could feel small metal things with our hands, but the keys were not there. At last a boy who was out to fish found them inside his net.","zh":"奶奶在海滩上把钥匙丢了。早饭一过我们就开始找。她在每条长椅下面翻，我沿着水边一路搜寻。舅舅上网查了失物招领处的信息，又给警察打了电话，他们答应去查。一位渔夫帮我们翻看船边的湿沙。我们用手能摸到些小金属件，但钥匙不在那儿。最后，一个出来钓鱼的男孩在网里找到了它。"},"unite":{"tw":[["join",2],["connect",0],["combine",0],["divide",1],["marry",3],["union",4],["unity",6],["club",3],["integrate",2]],"en":"Two small reading clubs decided to unite last spring. Each club had its own room, its own rules, and its own tea. To join them was easy in words and hard in practice. The new committee wanted to connect the two groups and combine the libraries, but not to divide the money unequally. The idea was to integrate the older readers with the younger ones. In the first month there were many long talks. Then a young couple who planned to marry asked if they could hold their party in the bigger hall. That evening the union felt real, and the unity was clear to everyone.","zh":"去年春天，两个小读书会决定合并。每个会都有自己的房间、自己的规矩、自己的茶。嘴上说合在一起容易，真做起来难。新成立的委员会想把两边连起来、把书库并起来，但不愿把钱分得不均。他们的想法是让年长的读者和年轻读者融到一起。头一个月开了很多长会。后来一对准备结婚的年轻人问，能不能把婚宴放在大一点的那个厅里办。那天晚上，这个联合终于有了实在的感觉。"},"satisfy":{"tw":[["satisfaction",4],["fill",0],["answer",3],["provide",2],["dissatisfy",1],["accept",6],["satisfactory",4],["meet",2],["cover",3],["fail",6],["fulfil",0]],"en":"The customer came back to the counter and said nothing we sold could satisfy her. She had asked the shop to provide a refund, and we had tried to meet her request, but our answer was not satisfactory. We could not fill the order in time, and that seemed to dissatisfy her even more. The manager offered to cover the cost of a new part herself. The woman would not accept it at first. In the end we did not fail her. We did fulfil the promise and gave her a small gift, which brought a quiet satisfaction to everyone at the till. She finally smiled and left.","zh":"那位顾客回到柜台前，说我们卖的任何东西都让她满意不了。她要求店里退款，我们也尽量满足了她的要求，可我们的答复并不能叫她满意。我们没能按时交货，这好像让她更不痛快。经理提出由她本人垫付一个新零件的钱。那女人起初不肯接受。最后我们到底没让她失望。我们还是兑现了承诺，送了她一件小礼物，这让收银台边的每个人都生出一份淡淡的满足。她终于笑了笑，走了。"},"stretch":{"tw":[["stretcher",4],["load",0],["tree",3],["grow",2],["shrink",1],["rough",6],["reach",0],["crane",3],["move",2],["edge",6],["extend",0]],"en":"On the building site a heavy load hung from the crane above the road. The workers had to stretch a net over the edge before they could move it. One man reached up to feel the rough rope, and the tree beside the wall seemed to grow taller in the light. My father said the steel would shrink in the cold and the whole thing might slip. He stretched his back and took a slow breath. A stretcher waited near the gate, just in case. He said they should extend the fence a little further. Nobody in the crew argued with him.","zh":"工地上，一捆重物吊在路面上方的吊车上。工人们得先在边上拉一张网，才能挪动它。一个人伸手去摸那根粗绳，墙边那棵树在光里好像长高了。我爸说天一冷钢就会缩，整捆东西说不定会滑下来。他伸了伸背，慢慢吸了口气。担架就搁在大门边，以防万一。他说栅栏该再往外延一点。队里没人跟他争。"},"surface":{"tw":[["superficial",4],["coat",0],["bed",3],["appear",2],["overhead",1],["layer",6],["open",0],["board",3],["cover",2],["visible",6],["rise",0]],"en":"By morning the surface of the lake had turned to ice, and a thin layer of snow lay on top of it. A grey coat of cloud hung overhead, and the far bank was barely visible. My sister sat on a wooden board at the open edge and watched a fish appear under the ice. Her worry was only superficial, she said, and she would not cover it up. She bent low, as if the cold bed of the water could tell her something. Slowly the sun began to rise, and the whole field of ice began to shine. It was very quiet.","zh":"到早上，湖面已经结成了冰，冰上薄薄铺了一层雪。头顶压着一层灰云，对岸几乎看不清。我妹妹坐在敞开的冰边一块木板上，看着一条鱼在冰下露出来。她说她的担心只是表面的，她也不打算遮掩。她弯下腰去，好像水底那冰冷的床能告诉她些什么。太阳慢慢升起来，整片冰面开始发亮。四下很静。"},"silence":{"tw":[["silent",4],["quiet",0],["mum",3],["condition",2],["sound",1],["hear",6],["hush",3],["gag",3],["suppress",2],["outrage",6]],"en":"After the doctor spoke, a long silence filled the little room, and no one could find a sound to break it. My mother sat silent with her hands in her lap. She had promised to keep mum about the news until the weekend. The condition of my grandmother was not good, and the family tried to hush the children so she could rest. I could hear only the clock. Someone tried to suppress a small cough, and a gag of fear rose in my own throat. Later, in the car, my father spoke with a quiet outrage about the cost of the medicine.","zh":"医生说完之后，一阵长久的沉默填满了那间小屋，谁也找不出一句话来打破它。我妈坐着不吭声，双手放在膝上。她答应过这事先不声张，等到了周末再说。我奶奶的状况不好，家里人尽量让孩子们安静下来，好让她歇着。我只听得见那只钟。有人忍着不出声地咳了一下，一股恐惧堵在我自己的喉咙口。后来在车里，我爸压着嗓子，愤愤地说了说那药有多贵。"},"standard":{"tw":[["stand",4],["measure",0],["scale",3],["post",2],["system",6],["stock",0],["gauge",3],["flag",2],["model",6],["banner",0]],"en":"The factory had to meet a new standard for clean air, and the managers did not like it. A tall post stood at the gate with a white flag, and beside it hung a banner about the rules. They would stand outside for hours and argue about the scale of the cost. The old system had no gauge for smoke, and the stock of spare parts was low. My uncle said the new model of burner would change everything. He had to measure the smoke himself each morning and write it in a book. In the end they agreed, though not with much joy.","zh":"厂子得达到一项新的清洁空气标准，管理层不乐意。大门边立着一根高高的柱子，上面挂着一面白旗，旁边还挂着一条写着规定的横幅。他们会在外面站上好几个钟头，争论这代价有多大。老系统没有测烟的仪表，备件的库存也见底了。我叔说新款的燃烧器会把一切都改变。他得每天早上自己去测烟，再记在本子上。最后他们还是答应了，虽然并不太情愿。"},"stock":{"tw":[["stocking",4],["blood",0],["family",3],["flower",2],["market",6],["carry",0],["issue",3],["grow",2],["price",6],["line",0]],"en":"At the winter market the old couple sold what they could from a small stall. Their stock of wool was nearly gone, and only one pair of stockings was left on the line. The price of a single flower had gone up that week, and people walked past without a word. My aunt said the stall had been in their family for years, and the same blood ran in all of them. She would carry a basket for them when the crowd grew thick. She said the shop issue was simple: too much cold, too few buyers. Then she bought the last pair herself.","zh":"冬天的集市上，那对老夫妻在个小摊上卖着能卖的东西。他们的羊毛存货快没了，绳上只剩下一双长袜。那一周一朵花的价格也涨了，人们一声不响地走过去。我姑妈说这个摊子在他們家已经传了好些年，一家人身上流着一样的血。人多起来时，她会帮他们拎篮子。她说店里的难处很简单：天太冷，买主太少。然后她把最后那双袜子自己买了下来。"},"stomach":{"tw":[["gastric",4],["bear",0],["accept",3],["permit",2],["throat",6],["stand",0],["pay",3],["digest",2],["pain",6],["support",0]],"en":"My uncle could not bear rich food, and his stomach had troubled him for years. The doctor said the gastric problem was not serious, but he had to accept a plainer diet. He was not allowed to eat late, and the clinic would not permit strong coffee. Sometimes the pain ran up from his stomach to his throat, and he had to stand still until it passed. He would pay for the medicine himself and take it with water before bed. He said his only support was his wife, who cooked for him every day. Slowly his body learned to digest food again.","zh":"我叔受不了油腻的东西，胃已经折腾了他好些年。医生说这胃上的毛病不严重，可他得接受吃得清淡些。他不许吃得太晚，诊所也不让他喝浓咖啡。有时候疼从胃一直窜到喉咙，他只能站住不动，等它过去。药他自己掏钱买，睡前就着水喝下。他说他唯一的依靠是他老婆，天天给他做饭。慢慢地，身体又学会了消化。"},"tone":{"tw":[["tonic",4],["feel",0],["register",3],["sound",2],["contrast",6],["look",0],["harmonic",3],["talk",2],["voice",6],["note",3]],"en":"My teacher would talk about the tone of a voice the way other people talk about the weather. She said a warm note could calm a room, while a cold one would set a hard contrast. She asked me to feel the sound in my chest before I sang, and to keep it in the lower register. One evening a tonic chord filled the hall, and the harmonic line above it seemed to float. She told me to look at the wall, not at the crowd. By the end my own tone had changed, and I could hear it. It was a small thing, but it mattered.","zh":"我的老师谈起嗓音的音色，就像别人谈天气一样。她说一个温暖的音能安抚一整屋子人，而一个冷音会形成强烈的对比。她让我唱之前在胸腔里感受那个音，把它压在中低音区。有天晚上一个大调主和弦灌满了整个大厅，它上面的泛音线条仿佛浮了起来。她叫我看墙，别看观众。到末尾我自己的音色变了，我自己都听得出来。这是件小事，却很要紧。"},"unit":{"tw":[["unify",4],["whole",2],["couple",3],["object",2],["division",6],["unitary",4],["family",3],["component",6]],"en":"The engineers designed a small unit that could heat a room on its own. Its main component was a thin metal plate, and the whole thing weighed less than a bag of flour. Two of them together could unify the heating of a large room, and a couple of them were enough for a flat. One division of the factory made the plate, another made the case. The designers wanted a unitary system, not a set of parts. I asked what object they had in mind, and the head of the team said simply: a warm family on a cold night.","zh":"工程师们设计了一台能自己给一间屋供暖的小装置。它的主要部件是一片薄薄的金属板，整个东西比一袋面粉还轻。两台合起来就能统一给一间大屋供暖，一套公寓有两台就够了。厂里一个部门做那块金属板，另一个部门做外壳。设计者想要的是一个统一的系统，而不是一堆零件。我问他们心里的目标是什么，组长只说了一句：冷夜里一个暖和的家。"},"seed":{"tw":[["seedy",4],["sow",0],["broadcast",3],["bear",2],["germ",0],["grain",3],["rate",2],["compatriot",6]],"en":"In spring my grandfather would sow the first seed in the wet soil and then broadcast the rest by hand. He said a single grain had to bear a whole field of wheat. Once a seedy patch near the fence worried him, and he had to raise the rate of water. A compatriot from the next farm came to help, and they talked about the hidden germ of a new, stronger plant. He would not waste a single one. At dusk he closed the gate and said the field was his only real wealth. It had been a good, long year.","zh":"春天里，我爷爷会在湿土里先播下第一粒种子，其余的用手撒开。他说，一粒谷子将来得养出一整片麦子。有一回篱笆边上一块地方长得稀稀拉拉，让他犯了愁，他只好把浇水的量加大。隔壁农场的一个同乡来帮忙，两人聊起一种更壮实的新庄稼藏着的胚芽。他一粒也不肯浪费。天擦黑时他关上栅门，说这片地是他唯一真正的家底。这一年，又长又好。"},"sew":{"tw":[["sewer",4],["stitch",0],["gather",3],["fashion",2],["embroider",6],["tailor",0],["tick",3],["fasten",2],["weave",6]],"en":"My grandmother liked to sew by the window every afternoon, and she was a quick, patient sewer. She would stitch a hem in minutes, gather the cloth in her lap, and then embroider a small flower on the collar. In her youth she had worked for a tailor and learned the fashion of that time. She would fasten each button with a firm knot and weave a thin thread through the seam. I used to sit and listen to the clock tick. She said a good coat should outlive the person who made it. That room was always warm and full of light.","zh":"我奶奶喜欢每天下午在窗边做针线，她是个又快又有耐心的缝衣人。几分钟就能缝好一道裙边，把布拢在膝上，再在领口绣一朵小花。她年轻时给一个裁缝干过活，学会了那时的样式。她会用结实的结把每颗扣子钉牢，再用细线从缝里穿过去。我常坐在旁边听钟滴答地走。她说，一件好大衣该比做它的人活得还久。那间屋子总是暖融融的，满是光。"},"suck":{"tw":[["sucker",4],["blow",0],["blot",3],["drink",2],["bleed",6],["draw",2],["feed",2],["swallow",6],["nurse",0]],"en":"At the clinic a young nurse taught my sister how to feed her baby from a small cup. The infant would suck the milk slowly, then blow a soft bubble and swallow. My sister used a cloth to blot the drops on its chin. She had to draw the milk first into a thin glass tube. The nurse said the baby was a strong little sucker and would soon drink more. One small cut on its lip began to bleed, and we had to press it gently. Then the child fell asleep in her arms. The whole room was very quiet then.","zh":"在诊所里，一位年轻的护士教我妹妹怎么用小杯子喂孩子。婴儿会慢慢地把奶吸进去，再吹出一个小泡，然后咽下。我妹妹用一块布把滴到下巴上的奶点点擦掉。她得先把奶吸进一根细玻璃管里。护士说这孩子是个有力气的小吸奶嘴，很快就能喝得更多。孩子唇上有一道小口子开始流血，我们只好轻轻按住。后来孩子在她怀里睡着了。那会儿整间屋子都很静。"},"suspect":{"tw":[["suspicion",4],["distrust",0],["doubt",3],["guess",2],["arrest",6],["mistrust",0],["think",2],["witness",6],["surmise",0]],"en":"The police had one suspect, but the witness was not sure of his face. A quiet suspicion had grown in the street, and neighbours began to distrust everyone who passed. The officer had to guess how the man had left without being seen. He would not arrest anyone on a doubt alone. I think the whole town wanted an answer, and people began to mistrust even the newspaper. One old man offered to surmise what had happened, and his story sounded better than the truth. In the end they let the suspect go free. Nobody in the town was happy with that.","zh":"警方锁定了一个嫌疑人，可那位目击者认不准他的脸。街上悄悄生出一层疑心，邻居们开始猜忌每一个路过的人。警官只得推测那男人是怎么在没人看见的情况下离开的。光凭一点疑虑，他不肯抓人。我想整座镇子都想要个说法，人们连报纸都开始不信了。一位老人自告奋勇地揣度了一番经过，他讲的故事比真相还好听。最后他们还是把嫌疑人放了。镇上没人对此满意。"},"tower":{"tw":[["tow",4],["loom",0],["beacon",3],["boat",2],["gate",6],["tug",0],["rise",2],["roof",6],["predominate",0]],"en":"From the harbour you could see one tall tower rise above the roofs of the old town. A stone beacon stood at its top, and at night its light seemed to loom over the water. A small boat was coming in, and another ship had to tow it through the narrow gate. A tug pulled the ropes tight, and the whole crowd went quiet. In that grey light the tower seemed to predominate over everything else on the shore. My father said that in a storm it was the only thing a sailor could trust. It had stood there for years.","zh":"从港口望过去，能看见一座高塔从老镇的屋顶间拔起来。塔顶立着一座石头灯塔，夜里它的光像罩在水面上。一条小船正在进港，另一条船得拖着它穿过那道窄窄的闸口。一艘拖轮把缆绳拉紧，人群一下静了下来。在那片灰光里，这座塔像是压过了岸上的一切。我爸说，遇上风暴时，它是水手唯一能信的东西。它在那儿立了好多年了。"},"trial":{"tw":[["try",4],["run",0],["fire",3],["attempt",2],["arrest",6],["test",0],["audition",3],["contest",2],["court",6]],"en":"The trial lasted three long days, and the whole court was tired. The lawyer would try again and again to test each witness, and once he made a bold attempt to change the story. A fire in a warehouse had started it all, and the police had made one arrest that night. The judge let the young reporter run a short audition of the tape for the room. It was not a contest, he said, but a search for the truth. By the end nobody could say for certain who had lit the match. The room stayed very quiet for a long time.","zh":"这场审判开了长长的三天，整个法庭都累了。律师一遍又一遍地试着盘问每个证人，有一回还大胆地想把说法整个翻过来。一切起于一座仓库里的火，那晚警方抓了一个人。法官让那位年轻记者把录音带给屋里的人放了一小段。他说，这不是比赛，而是找真相。到最后谁也说不准是谁点的火。屋里静了很久很久。"},"wire":{"tw":[["wiry",4],["cable",3],["filament",3],["adapt",2],["rope",6],["telegraph",0],["message",2],["mesh",6],["telegram",0]],"en":"An old telegraph office still stood at the end of the street, and a single wire ran from its roof to a wooden pole. Inside, a thin filament glowed above the desk, and a heavy cable lay coiled near the door. The clerk had to adapt an old machine to send a message in the new code. He would write each telegram by hand, then check it twice. A small rope and a metal mesh kept the window shut. His hands were thin and wiry from years of work. He said the wire carried more truth than any newspaper. I believed him.","zh":"街尽头还立着一间旧电报房，一根电线从房顶拉到一根木杆上。屋里，一根细细的灯丝在桌上方亮着，一条粗电缆盘在门边。职员得改装一台旧机器，好按新电码发消息。他会把每份电报手写下来，再核对两遍。一小段绳子和一层铁丝网把窗户掩住。多年的活儿让他的手又瘦又筋道。他说这电线捎来的真相，比哪份报纸都多。我信他。"},"respect":{"tw":[["honour",0],["court",3],["accept",2],["disrespect",1],["desire",6],["observe",0],["admire",3],["see",2],["recognize",6],["regard",0]],"en":"My grandfather always said that we should respect people who worked with their hands. He held a quiet regard for the old carpenter, and he would honour anyone who kept a promise. When a young man showed disrespect to his teacher, my grandfather would not accept it. He would observe the boy for a while, then speak to him alone. I began to admire him for that. You could see the change in the boy, and I came to recognize the same patience in myself. He had no desire for praise. In the end the neighbours gathered in the court behind the house and shared his view.","zh":"我爷爷总说，我们该尊敬那些靠一双手吃饭的人。他对那位老木匠怀着一种安静的敬意，谁守信用他就敬重谁。要是哪个年轻人对老师不敬，我爷爷绝不肯答应。他会先看看那孩子一阵，再单独跟他说话。我因此开始佩服他。那孩子身上的变化看得出来，我也慢慢在自己身上认出了同样的耐性。他并不图人夸。到头来，邻居们都聚到屋后的院子里，跟他是同一个看法。"},"rush":{"tw":[["charge",3],["tear",3],["act",2],["delay",1],["stop",6],["hurry",0],["dash",3],["doctor",2],["drive",6],["kick",0]],"en":"Every morning there was a rush at the station, and people would hurry past one another without a word. A man in a dark coat began to dash for the train, and a woman had to act fast to stop her case from falling. A loud charge of feet filled the hall. One traveller let out a small tear of anger at the delay. A doctor, late for a shift, asked the driver to drive a little faster. A boy gave the door a kick when it would not open. In the end the train left ten minutes late. Nobody said sorry.","zh":"每天早上车站里都是一阵忙乱，人们一句话不说就从彼此身边匆匆挤过去。一个穿深色外套的男人开始朝火车冲，一个女人只好赶紧出手，别让箱子摔下去。大厅里一片急促的脚步声。一位旅客因为延误，气出了一小滴眼泪。一位上班要迟到的医生叫司机再开快一点。一个男孩见门打不开，踢了它一脚。最后火车晚了十分钟才开。没人说声抱歉。"},"separate":{"tw":[["break",3],["chip",3],["change",2],["joint",1],["several",6],["count",3],["move",2],["various",6],["tell",0]],"en":"My mother had to separate the old cups from the new ones before the guests came. Several of them had a small chip, and she did not want to break a good set. She would count them twice, then move the boxes into the hall. The change of plan meant she had to do it all again. A joint of the shelf had come loose, and the cups could fall at any moment. She tried to tell me which ones were the best, but there were various sizes and I lost track. In the end we kept them all together anyway.","zh":"客人来之前，我妈得把旧杯子跟新的分开。有好几只都崩了个小口，她又不想弄坏一套好杯子。她会数上两遍，再把箱子挪到门厅里。计划一变，这事她就得重来一遍。架子上有一处接缝松了，杯子随时可能掉下来。她想告诉我是哪几只最好，可大小不一，我听着听着就糊涂了。最后还是把它们全搁在一起了。"},"sink":{"tw":[["drop",2],["sag",3],["move",2],["float",1],["drain",6],["pass",0],["submerge",3],["collapse",2],["bottom",6],["settle",3]],"en":"The kitchen sink was old, and one morning the water refused to drain away. A single drop fell from the tap, then a slow stream began to sag toward the bottom of the bowl. My father had to move the whole unit out to reach the pipe. He said a loose joint could collapse under the weight. He let the cloth submerge in a bucket of hot water, then watched the dirt float up. Time seemed to pass slowly as he worked. At last the water began to settle and the sink drained clean again. It was a quiet, slow afternoon at home.","zh":"厨房的水槽旧了，一天早上水怎么也排不下去。水龙头滴下一滴水，接着一股细细的水流开始往盆底沉慢地淌去。我爸只得把整个家伙挪出来，够到那根管子。他说接缝要是松了，承不住重量会塌。他把布浸在一桶热水里，看着脏东西浮上来。他干着活，时间好像过得很慢。到最后，水沉下去了，水槽又排得干干净净。家里这个下午，安静又漫长。"},"solid":{"tw":[["square",0],["glass",3],["matter",2],["liquid",1],["consistent",6],["strong",0],["block",3],["shape",2],["balance",6],["whole",0]],"en":"The engineers wanted a solid base for the new machine, so they poured a square block of concrete. It had to hold its shape under a heavy load, and the glass panel above it had to stay level. They tested how the matter behaved when it changed from a liquid to a solid state. The result had to be consistent, and the whole design had to balance on four points. A strong frame would keep it steady. My uncle said the base looked plain, but it would outlast the machine on top of it. It did, and it is still standing today.","zh":"工程师们想给新机器造一个结实的地基，于是浇了一块方形的混凝土。它得在重压下保持形状，上面的玻璃板还得保持水平。他们试验了这种物质从液体变成固体时的表现。结果必须前后一致，整个设计得在四个支点上保持平衡。一个坚固的框架能让它稳稳当当。我叔说这地基看着不起眼，可它比上面那台机器还耐用。果然如此，到今天它还立着。"},"spread":{"tw":[["open",0],["carry",3],["cover",2],["gather",1],["through",6],["broadcast",0],["catch",3],["farm",2],["across",6],["circulate",0]],"en":"The news of the fire began to spread across the whole valley before noon. A neighbour would carry it from farm to farm, and another would broadcast it on the small local radio. People began to gather at the open gate and to cover their faces from the smoke. The story seemed to circulate faster than the wind. I had to catch my breath when I heard how far it had gone. By evening everyone knew, and nothing could stop it. A dry summer had helped it spread through the fields. It was a strange day, and the whole valley talked of nothing else.","zh":"中午之前，起火的消息就开始传遍整个山谷。一个邻居把它从一个农场带到另一个农场，另一个邻居则在本地的小电台上播了出去。人们开始聚到敞开的大门口，捂住脸挡烟。这消息传得好像比风还快。听说它传了那么远，我倒吸了一口气。到傍晚人人都知道了，什么也拦不住。一个干燥的夏天帮着它一路烧过田里。那是奇怪的一天，整个山谷都在谈这一件事。"},"suffer":{"tw":[["bear",0],["accept",3],["experience",2],["enjoy",1],["risk",6],["hurt",0],["catch",3],["feel",2],["cause",6],["lose",0]],"en":"My aunt would suffer from bad knees for years, and she could not bear to sit for long. She had to accept that she could no longer enjoy a long walk in the hills. She had once been a nurse, and she knew the risk of a fall better than anyone. When the pain would hurt most, she would catch her breath and feel the cold floor under her feet. Slowly she began to lose the fear of asking for help. The doctor could never name the cause, and in time she stopped asking. It was an experience she said she would not wish on anyone. It was a hard thing to watch, and we tried to help.","zh":"我姑妈膝盖不好，受了好些年的罪，坐久了她都忍着。她只得认了，再也不能享受在山里走远路。她从前当过护士，摔一跤有多危险，她比谁都清楚。疼得最厉害的时候，她会倒吸一口气，感觉脚底冰凉的地板。慢慢地，她不再那么怕开口求人了。医生始终说不清病因，后来她也就不问了。她说这种滋味，她不愿让任何人尝。看着实在难受，我们也尽量帮衬。"},"royal":{"tw":[["monarch",4],["purple",0],["sail",2],["queen",6],["imperial",0],["stag",2],["crown",6],["majestic",0]],"en":"The old palace on the hill still had a royal look, though no monarch had lived there for years. In the main hall a portrait showed a queen in a purple dress, with a small crown on her head and a stag at her feet. A guide told us the family had once been part of an imperial court that stretched far across the land. The stair was majestic, and it made me quiet. Outside, a boat would sail past the wall each morning with visitors. I stood there a long time and thought about how ordinary those people must have felt inside all that gold.","zh":"山上那座旧宫殿还带着王室的气派，虽然好些年没有君主住在里面了。正厅里有一幅画像，画的是一位穿紫衣的王后，头戴小皇冠，脚边站着一头雄鹿。导游说这家人当年属于一个疆域辽阔的帝国宫廷。那道楼梯很壮观，看得我说不出话。外面每天早上都有船载着游客从墙外驶过。我在那儿站了很久，想着那些人住在满屋金子里，心里大概也就是平常人的感觉。"},"speech":{"tw":[["speak",4],["address",3],["conversation",3],["faculty",2],["remark",6],["language",0],["aside",3],["lecture",0]],"en":"The head teacher gave a short speech at the end of term, and the whole hall went quiet. She did not speak about marks or rules; she talked about the small things we would remember. Then she turned to the students and made a kind remark about the ones who had helped others. I could not follow every address to the parents, but I understood her main point. Her language was simple, and there was no lecture in it, only a warm conversation. Once, in an aside the microphone caught, she told a teacher she was tired. The faculty smiled, and so did we.","zh":"学期末校长作了个短短的演讲，整个礼堂都静了下来。她没讲分数和规矩，说的是我们以后会记住的那些小事。然后她转向学生，对那些帮过别人的人说了句好话。她向家长致辞的每一句我没全听懂，但她的主旨我明白。她的语言很简单，里面没有说教，只有一场亲切的交谈。有一次麦克风没能掐掉她的一句旁白，她跟一位老师说累了。老师们都笑了，我们也笑了。"},"suspicion":{"tw":[["suspect",4],["misgiving",0],["heart",3],["doubt",2],["complicity",6],["mistrust",0],["cloud",3],["conspiracy",6]],"en":"There was a suspicion in the office after the money box was found open. At first it was only doubt, a quiet mistrust that nobody would say out loud. Then a cloud seemed to settle over the whole floor, and people stopped leaving their desks. The manager began to suspect the new man, though he had no proof of complicity. I had my own misgiving: the lock had been broken from inside. Someone whispered about a conspiracy, and that word did more harm than the missing money. In my heart I knew it was only a mistake, but by then nobody was listening.","zh":"钱箱被发现敞着以后，办公室里就有了疑心。起初只是怀疑，一种谁都不肯说出口的暗暗不信任。后来一片阴云好像罩住了整层楼，大家连座位都不肯离开。经理开始怀疑那个新来的，尽管没有任何证据说明他参与其中。我自己也有个疑虑：锁是从里头弄坏的。有人低声说这是合谋，这个词带来的伤害比丢的那点钱还大。我心里清楚那不过是个失误，可那时候已经没人听得进去了。"},"union":{"tw":[["unite",4],["join",0],["league",3],["council",6],["federal",0],["coalition",3],["alliance",6],["matrimony",0]],"en":"When the factory cut our hours, the workers decided to form a union. At first we were only a loose group, but we soon learned to unite and join our voices. We called a meeting in the old hall and asked the council for help. A league of small shops in the same street gave us money. Some wanted a wider alliance with other trades, even a federal one that would reach the next town. My father, who had never joined anything, signed the paper. He said it was not a coalition for power but a promise, almost like matrimony, between people who worked side by side.","zh":"厂里削减工时以后，工人们决定成立一个工会。起初我们只是一盘散沙，可很快就学会了联合起来，把声音凑成一股。我们在旧礼堂开了个会，还向市议会求助。同一条街上一些小店组成的同业联盟给了我们钱。有人想跟别的行当结成更大的联盟，甚至是能延伸到邻镇的联邦式组织。我爸从来没参加过任何组织，这次也签了字。他说这不是为了权势结成的同盟，而是一个承诺，几乎像婚姻一样，发生在并肩干活的人之间。"},"result":{"tw":[["answer",0],["change",3],["happen",2],["due",6],["issue",0],["deal",3],["produce",2],["however",6],["lead",3]],"en":"The result of the test came by post on a wet morning. My answer to the last question had been wrong, and the small change in my mark was a surprise. Nobody could explain what had happened, and the issue was clear: I had not read the page carefully. The teacher said the whole thing was due to a lack of sleep. However, she did not want to deal with it that day. She told me to produce a better paper next time, and that one good week could lead to a new habit.","zh":"成绩是一个下雨的早上寄来的。我最后一道题的答案是错的，分数那点小小的变化让我吃了一惊。谁也说不清到底怎么回事，问题很明白：我没仔细看那一页。老师说，这一切都是因为睡眠不够。不过她那天不想谈这事。她让我下次交一份更好的卷子，还说好好坚持一个星期就能养成新习惯。"},"root":{"tw":[["base",0],["home",3],["dig",2],["stem",6],["settle",0],["spring",3],["form",2],["leaf",6],["origin",0]],"en":"The old tree by our gate had a root the size of an arm. My father had to dig around it before he could settle the new fence in place. He said the base of the tree was older than the house, and its origin went back to a seed his grandmother had planted. In spring a thin stem rises from the ground, and a green leaf opens above it. The root takes the form of a hand, he said, and holds the soil like home. I never forgot that. I still look at it when I pass the gate.","zh":"我们家门口那棵老树有条胳膊粗的根。爸爸得先在它周围挖开，才能把新篱笆安稳。他说这树比房子还老，源头要追到他奶奶种下的一颗种子。春天里，一根细茎从地里冒出来，上面展开一片绿叶。他说这树根长得像一只手，像护家一样攥着泥土。这话我一直没忘。每次经过门口，我还会看它一眼。"},"rope":{"tw":[["circle",0],["cable",3],["line",2],["thread",6],["leash",0],["brace",3],["tie",2],["strap",6],["roach",0]],"en":"At the river my uncle took a thick rope from the boat and made a wide circle on the grass. He tied one end to a post and let the other line float. A thin thread of weed climbed the cable beside the pier, and a small roach swam near the surface. He showed me how to brace my feet and pull, and how to loop the strap over my shoulder. A dog on a leash barked at the water. That was the whole trick, he said, and I understood it at last.","zh":"在河边，叔叔从船上拿下一根粗绳，在草地上盘了个大圈。他把一头系在木桩上，让另一头的绳子漂着。一缕细水草顺着码头边的钢缆往上爬，一条小拟鲤贴着水面游。他教我怎么蹬稳脚发力，怎么把带子套上肩膀。一只拴着绳的狗冲着水叫。他说诀窍就在这儿，我这才弄明白。"},"row":{"tw":[["course",0],["pull",3],["boat",2],["end",6],["quarrel",0],["feather",3],["line",2],["break",6],["wrangle",0]],"en":"We took a boat out in the late afternoon and began to row across the lake. My sister pulled on one side, I pulled on the other, and the little craft moved in a slow line. At the far end a row of small houses stood along the shore, and birds left a single feather on the water. We kept a straight course until a quarrel began about who was stronger, which turned into a long wrangle. Then I heard something break under the seat. We stopped, laughed, and rowed back in silence.","zh":"后半晌我们划船出去，开始横穿湖面。姐姐拉一边，我拉另一边，小船慢慢走成一条直线。远远的那头，岸边立着一排小屋，水面上鸟儿留下一根羽毛。我们本来航向很直，后来为谁力气大争了起来，吵成了一场长架。接着我听见座位底下有什么响了。我们停下来，笑了笑，默默划了回去。"},"rub":{"tw":[["scratch",0],["worry",3],["touch",2],["sprinkle",6],["wipe",3],["brush",3],["contact",2],["discard",6],["fray",0]],"en":"My hands were cold, so I began to rub them together over the stove. The skin felt rough where the wood had left a scratch, and a small fray appeared on my sleeve. I did not want to worry my mother, so I wiped the surface of the table with a cloth and brushed the crumbs away. She came in, gave my shoulder a light touch, and asked me to sprinkle salt on the soup. I had to discard the burnt bread and start again. It was a small contact with real work, and I liked it.","zh":"我手很冷，就在炉子上搓了起来。木头刮过的地方皮肤发糙，袖子上也磨出了一小团毛边。我不想让妈妈操心，就拿布把桌面擦干净，又把面包屑扫掉。她进来，轻轻碰了下我的肩膀，让我往汤里撒点盐。我只好把烤糊的面包扔掉，重新来。这算是跟真正的活儿打了个照面，我挺喜欢。"},"ruin":{"tw":[["break",3],["burn",3],["destruction",2],["verge",6],["destroy",0],["finish",3],["failure",2],["haunt",6],["smash",0]],"en":"The old mill by the stream was already a ruin when I was a child. A fire had begun one night and seemed to burn for days, leaving nothing but black wood and broken stone. People said the destruction came from a lamp left near dry grass, and a single careless act was enough to destroy the whole roof. A man stood on the verge of tears and watched them smash a wall to stop the flames. He could not finish his sentence. The failure stayed with him for years, and the place still seemed to haunt the lane.","zh":"我还是孩子的时候，溪边那座老磨坊就已经是一片废墟了。有天夜里起了火，烧了好几天，只剩烧黑的木头和碎石头。人们说那场毁坏是挨着干草放的灯引起的，一个不小心的举动就足以毁掉整个屋顶。一个男人含着泪站在边上，看着他们砸墙去挡火。他一句话都说不完整。那次失手他记了好多年，那地方至今仍像在巷子里作祟。"},"score":{"tw":[["hit",0],["break",3],["reason",2],["goal",6],["mark",0],["game",3],["record",2],["straight",6],["account",0]],"en":"By half time the score was two to one. Our best player made a hit that sent the ball straight past the keeper, and the whole crowd stood up. There was no clear reason for the goal, only luck and a fast run. The coach kept a mark on a small board and wrote down every game in his record book. He said we should break the habit of shouting at one another. At the end he had a long account of our mistakes. The final score did not matter as much as the way we played.","zh":"半场时比分是二比一。我们最好的球员一脚打门，球直直从守门员身边飞过，全场都站了起来。那个进球没什么道理可言，就是运气加一次快跑。教练在小板上做了个记号，把每场比赛都记在本子上。他说我们得改掉互相喊叫的毛病。最后他列了一长串我们的失误。终场比分倒不如我们踢球的样子要紧。"},"scratch":{"tw":[["bread",0],["character",3],["line",2],["roll",6],["mark",0],["score",3],["noise",2],["stuff",6],["start",0]],"en":"A thin line of red marked my arm where the cat had left a scratch. I did not cry, but I made a small noise and pulled my sleeve down. My grandmother cut a roll of bread and put it on the table. She said a scratch on the skin is nothing next to a mark on the character. She drew a little face on paper to make me laugh, then wiped it out and let me start again. She said she would score my next drawing when I was ready. I rolled the pencil between my fingers. There was flour on the stuff in the bowl, and the morning went on.","zh":"猫抓过的地方，我胳膊上留下了一道细细的红痕。我没哭，只是轻轻出了点声，把袖子拉了下来。奶奶切了个面包卷放到桌上。她说皮肤上的一道抓痕，比起品行上的污点算不了什么。她在纸上画了个小脸逗我笑，又擦掉让我重画。她说等我准备好了，就给我的下一张画打分。我把铅笔在手指间转来转去。盆里那团面还沾着面粉，那个上午就这么过去了。"},"scream":{"tw":[["call",0],["howl",3],["joke",2],["laugh",6],["cry",2],["shriek",3],["noise",2],["kiss",6],["shout",2]],"en":"A scream came from the back of the house, and my mother ran to the door. It was only my aunt, who had seen a mouse and let out a long call for help. She would shriek at every small thing, and then howl with laughter at herself. My uncle made a joke about it, and we all began to laugh until our eyes were wet. I had to shout to be heard over the noise. My mother gave me a kiss and told me to go back to bed. My little sister began to cry, but not from fear. After that the night was quiet.","zh":"屋子后面传来一声尖叫，妈妈赶紧跑到门口。原来只是姑姑，她看见一只老鼠，拉长嗓子喊救命。她什么事都爱尖叫，喊完又自己笑得直不起腰。叔叔拿这事开了个玩笑，我们全都笑到眼睛发潮。噪音太大，我得喊才能让人听见。妈妈亲了我一下，叫我回床上睡。我妹妹哭了起来，可不是因为害怕。那之后，夜里就静了。"},"screen":{"tw":[["cover",0],["background",3],["check",2],["camera",6],["test",0],["shade",3],["choose",2],["feature",6],["blind",3]],"en":"The screen on my phone went dark while I was checking a photo. I had to cover it with my hand to keep out the sun, because the glass gave no shade at all. In the background of the picture I could see a blind pulled down over the window. I tried to choose a better shot with the camera, then ran a simple test on the setting. The new feature let me lift the light and dark parts apart, like a fine screen. When it worked, the whole image seemed to open.","zh":"我正查看一张照片时，手机屏幕黑了。我只好用手遮住它挡太阳，因为那玻璃一点都不遮光。照片的背景里，我能看见窗户上拉下的百叶帘。我试着用相机挑一张更好的，又对设置做了个简单的测试。新功能能把明暗分开，像一张细密的筛子。它一奏效，整张图好像都打开了。"},"screw":{"tw":[["bed",0],["worm",3],["beat",2],["crank",6],["love",0],["bolt",3],["wheel",6],["bang",0]],"en":"He had to fix the old bed, so he took a screw, a bolt, and a small wheel from a tin. The wooden frame would bang and rattle whenever anyone sat down, and the noise beat against the wall all night. He turned the crank of his old drill with one hand, then tightened the metal with the other. A thin worm of sawdust fell to the floor. He said he loved a neat job, and this one was close. By eight the bed stood still, and nobody could hear it move.","zh":"他得修那张旧床，就从铁盒里拿出一颗螺钉、一根螺栓和一个小轮子。那木架子谁一坐上去就砰砰响，声音整晚撞着墙。他一只手摇着旧钻的曲柄，另一只手把铁件拧紧。一缕细细的木屑落到地上。他说他就爱干利落的活儿，这次也算不上差。到八点，床稳稳当当，谁都听不见它响了。"},"section":{"tw":[["department",0],["class",2],["branch",6],["division",0],["game",3],["cut",2],["main",6],["segment",0]],"en":"The old stadium was divided into sections, and our seats were in the back part of one. A girl in my class led us through the main gate and past the department that sold drinks. She worked for a small branch of the club and knew every division of the ground. We watched a game from high up, and with a small cut of my thumb I marked the score on my hand. A thin segment of light fell across the seats as the sun went down. No one wanted to leave.","zh":"这座老体育场分成好几个区，我们的座位在最靠后的一个区里。班里一个女孩带我们从正门进去，路过卖饮料的那个部门。她替俱乐部的一个小分部做事，场地每一块她都清楚。我们坐在高处看球，手指被划了个小口子，我就在手上记比分。太阳落下时，一道细细的光横铺在座位上。谁都不想走。"},"seek":{"tw":[["try",0],["feel",3],["act",2],["accept",6],["attempt",0],["fight",3],["travel",2],["allow",6],["search",0]],"en":"My aunt began to seek help when the pain in her back would not go away. At first she did not want to feel like a burden, and she would not allow anyone to take her to the doctor. Then she made a quiet attempt to act on her own and failed. My uncle said she had to fight her fear and accept the truth. She started to travel to the city twice a month, and each time she would search for a better answer. It was worth one more try, she said, and she was right.","zh":"背上的疼一直不好，姑姑这才开始去寻医问药。起初她不愿让自己像个拖累，也不让任何人带她去看病。后来她悄悄试着自己扛，结果不行。叔叔说她得跟害怕较劲，接受实情。她开始每月往城里跑两趟，每次都去打听有没有更好的办法。她说，值得再试一次，而她说对了。"},"sheet":{"tw":[["sail",0],["board",3],["cover",2],["rack",6],["plane",0],["film",3],["line",2],["bottom",6],["canvas",0]],"en":"At the top of the mast a white sail moved in the wind, and below it a thin cover of canvas kept the rain off the deck. My father pulled a clean sheet from the rack and laid it over the board that served as our table. A line of small boats went past, and a plane crossed the sky far above. He put a sheet of film over the window to keep the light out at night. Down at the bottom of the boat, near the water, everything smelled of salt.","zh":"桅杆顶上，一面白帆迎着风动，帆下面一层薄帆布替甲板挡着雨。爸爸从架子上抽出一张干净床单，铺在那块当桌子用的木板上。一列小船从旁边驶过，高远处有架飞机划过天空。他往窗户上贴了一张膜，夜里好挡光。船底挨着水的地方，什么东西都带着咸味。"},"shell":{"tw":[["beat",0],["boot",3],["hit",2],["mortar",6],["plate",0],["cheat",3],["gather",2],["ground",6],["scale",0]],"en":"On the beach I began to gather shells, and I put each one on a plate to see its shape. A small crab lived in one, and its hard shell was the colour of stone. My brother said he would beat me at the game, though he knew he could not cheat the sea. A boot print in the wet ground held a single drop of water. Near the rocks we found a piece of old mortar and a metal case that looked like a shell. A wave hit the rocks and wet my boots. At home I set them on a small scale, one by one.","zh":"在海滩上我开始捡贝壳，把每一个都放到盘子里看形状。有一只里面住着小蟹，那硬壳的颜色像石头。哥哥说这游戏他准赢我，尽管他知道自己骗不过海。湿地上一个靴印里积着一滴水。靠礁石那边，我们找到一块旧的砂浆和一截像炮弹壳的金属筒。一个浪打到礁石上，把我的靴子打湿了。回到家，我把它们一个一个放到小秤上称了称。"},"shift":{"tw":[["break",3],["back",3],["dress",2],["trend",6],["change",2],["carry",3],["key",2],["focus",6],["slip",0]],"en":"My mother worked the night shift at the hospital for six years. The change in her sleep was the hardest part, and she often had to carry her tired body back home at dawn. She would dress in the dark, take her key, and slip out before we woke. There was a clear trend in her mood each week: quiet on Monday, tired by Friday. At break she would sit with a cup of tea and try to focus on something small. Then, in spring, she asked for a day shift, and we began to see her again.","zh":"妈妈在医院上夜班，一上就是六年。最难熬的是作息颠倒，她常常得在拂晓时拖着疲惫的身子回家。她摸黑穿好衣服，拿上钥匙，趁我们没醒就溜出门。她每周的情绪都有个明显的走势：周一沉默，到周五就累透了。休息时她会端杯茶坐下，努力把心思放在一件小事上。后来春天她申请上白班，我们才又能常常见到她。"},"shine":{"tw":[["fall",0],["burn",3],["feel",2],["sparkle",6],["strike",0],["blaze",3],["happen",2],["bright",6],["polish",3]],"en":"In the late afternoon the shine on the sea made me feel warm inside. The sun seemed to burn low over the water and to strike the wet sand with a wide blaze of light. Small drops began to sparkle on the rocks, and the whole shore turned bright. Then the light started to fall behind the hills, and the colour went out of the sky. My father would polish the little boat until its side had the same shine. Anything might happen after dark, he said, but the evening was ours.","zh":"后半晌，海面上的波光让我心里发暖。太阳低低地悬在水上，像在燃烧，把湿沙子照成一大片火亮。岩石上的水珠开始闪起来，整条海岸都亮了。后来光开始往山后落，天色一点点褪去。爸爸总要把小船擦到船帮上也是那种光。他说天黑以后什么都可能发生，但这个黄昏是我们的。"},"shock":{"tw":[["blow",2],["startle",3],["fight",2],["sudden",6],["floor",0],["galvanize",3],["surprise",2],["pain",6],["impact",0]],"en":"The sudden news came as a shock to the whole street. A car had hit the wall at the corner, and the impact shook the floor of our house. My mother ran out, and the sight of the broken glass gave her a real startle. A man on the ground held his arm and did not hide the pain. The blow could have been much worse. That night the neighbours began a small fight about the speed of cars, and the talk seemed to galvanize them into asking for a new sign. It was a surprise to everyone.","zh":"那个突然的消息让整条街都震动了。一辆车撞上了街角的墙，冲击震得我们家地板直晃。妈妈跑了出去，一看见碎玻璃，她真的吓了一跳。地上那个男人抱着胳膊，没有掩饰疼痛。这一下本来可能严重得多。那天晚上邻居们为了车速的事吵了一小架，争论似乎把大家激了起来，纷纷要求加一块新路牌。所有人都很意外。"},"skirt":{"tw":[["bird",0],["fringe",3],["touch",2],["satin",6],["ring",0],["cloister",3],["avoid",2],["trousers",6],["duck",0]],"en":"The girl in the blue skirt stood near the window and did not touch her food. She wore a ring on one finger, and her trousers hung on the chair behind her. Outside, a duck crossed the yard and a bird sang from the wall. Her skirt had a thin fringe at the bottom, and the satin caught the light. She said she wanted to avoid the town and live near an old cloister, where the days were quiet. Her mother said nothing and cut the bread. It was one of those evenings that no one wanted to end.","zh":"穿蓝裙子的姑娘站在窗边，没碰自己的饭。她一个手指上戴着戒指，裤子搭在身后的椅子上。外面，一只鸭子穿过院子，一只鸟在墙头鸣叫。她裙子的下摆有一圈细细的流苏，缎面折着光。她说她想躲开这座城，住到一座旧回廊旁边去，那儿日子安静。她妈妈没说话，只是切面包。那是谁都不愿结束的一个晚上。"},"slide":{"tw":[["slip",0],["runway",3],["move",2],["plunge",6],["coast",0],["submarine",3],["travel",2],["tumble",6],["glide",2]],"en":"The children ran to the slide at the end of the yard and took turns going down. One of them would slip on the wet step and tumble into the grass with a shout. Down by the coast road, a car began to move slowly along the runway of the small airfield, then plunge toward the gate. A submarine could not glide through water like that, my uncle said, and he had travelled on one. He showed us a slide of the harbour on the wall. That afternoon nothing bad happened, and the light stayed soft.","zh":"孩子们跑到院子尽头的滑梯那儿，排队往下滑。总有一个会在湿台阶上滑一下，喊一声摔进草里。靠海边的公路上，一辆车开始沿小机场的跑道慢慢动，接着朝大门冲去。叔叔说，潜水艇可没法那样在水里滑行，他还在上面坐过。他在墙上给我们放了一张港口的幻灯片。那天下午什么坏事也没发生，光一直是柔的。"},"smart":{"tw":[["bright",0],["burn",3],["pain",2],["stupid",1],["intelligent",6],["fresh",0],["shoot",3],["savvy",6],["hurt",0]],"en":"My cousin is smart in a quiet way. She never says a stupid thing, and she is more intelligent than most people I know at work. When the machine broke, she found the small fault before anyone else. Her eyes were bright and sharp, and she has a fresh idea every week. She is also savvy about money, which is rare. Once she burned her hand on the pipe and did not let the pain show. She can shoot a photo of the fault and send it in a minute. She said a small hurt is nothing, and went straight back to the panel.","zh":"我表姐是那种不声不响的聪明。她从不讲蠢话，比我认识的多数同事都更有头脑。机器一出故障，她比谁都先找到那个小毛病。她眼睛又亮又利，每周都有新主意。她花钱还很精明，这很难得。有回她手被管子烫了，也没让疼露在脸上。她能把故障拍张照，一分钟就发出去。她说这点小伤不算什么，转身又回到操作台前。"},"smooth":{"tw":[["quiet",0],["file",3],["rid",2],["rough",1],["soft",6],["polish",0],["float",3],["thin",6],["shine",0]],"en":"The stone in my hand was smooth, worn by years of water. My father used a file to take the rough parts off a piece of wood, then a cloth to polish the surface until it began to shine. He said a good surface should feel neither thin nor heavy, just soft and even. The room was quiet except for that sound. He wanted to get rid of every mark. When he set the finished board in water, it would float for a moment, then settle. I kept the small stone in my pocket for years.","zh":"我手里那块石头很滑，是水磨了好多年磨出来的。爸爸用锉刀把一块木头上的粗糙部分锉掉，再用布把表面擦到发亮。他说好的表面既不薄也不沉，只是又软又匀。屋里很静，只有那个声音。他想把每一道痕都去掉。他把做好的木板放进水里，它会浮一下，再沉下去。那块小石头我在口袋里放了好多年。"},"snap":{"tw":[["catch",0],["die",3],["act",2],["pick",6],["photograph",0],["bounce",3],["break",2],["scramble",6],["shoot",0]],"en":"The branch began to snap under my foot. I had to catch the rail, or I would have fallen. My camera was in my bag, and I did not stop to photograph the view; I only wanted to climb down. A dry stick would break with a small sound, and a stone would bounce down the slope. Two birds began to scramble over a piece of bread, and one tried to shoot away with it. My uncle said a plant can die if you pick its leaves. I did not act on that advice, and I lost the flower.","zh":"脚下的树枝开始断裂。我赶紧抓住栏杆，不然就摔下去了。相机在包里，我没停下来拍那片景色，只想往下爬。干树枝断起来声音很轻，石子会顺着坡弹下去。两只鸟为一块面包争了起来，一只还想叼着飞走。叔叔说，摘叶子会把植物弄死。我没听这话，结果那朵花就没了。"},"soil":{"tw":[["dirty",0],["mud",3],["change",2],["moisture",6],["ground",0],["pollute",3],["earth",2],["water",6],["land",0]],"en":"The soil in our garden is dark and rich, and my grandmother says good earth should smell sweet after rain. She turns it over with a fork to keep the moisture in, though the work leaves her hands dirty with mud. In spring the ground is soft enough to hold a small pool of water. She would never let anyone pollute the land with old oil. The colour of the soil will change through the year, from black in winter to a pale brown in summer. Now and then a green shoot comes up where we did not plant one.","zh":"我们园子里的土又黑又肥，奶奶说好土下雨后该有股甜味。她用叉子翻土，好保住水分，这活儿干下来她双手沾满泥。春天土地软，能积起一小洼水。她绝不许人用废油把这块地弄脏。土的颜色一年里会变，冬天乌黑，夏天变成浅褐。偶尔在我们没种东西的地方，冒出一棵绿芽。"},"speed":{"tw":[["hurry",0],["run",3],["change",2],["distance",6],["race",0],["tear",3],["rate",2],["fast",6],["rush",0]],"en":"The speed of the small train was never high, but the distance it covered each day was long. My father would hurry to the station, then run the last part, and his rate of walking would change with his mood. Once he took part in a race along the track and had to tear his coat on a fence. He liked the fast trains best. There was always a rush at the gate at five, and he said the crowd pushed him like water. I never saw him angry, even when he missed it.","zh":"这趟小火车速度从来不高，可每天走的路程很长。爸爸会先催自己赶去车站，最后一段干脆跑起来，他走路的快慢跟着心情变。有一回他沿着轨道参加一场赛跑，还把外套在篱笆上划破了。他最喜欢快车。五点一到，门口总是一阵人流，他说那人群像水一样推着他走。就算误了车，我也没见过他发火。"},"spirit":{"tw":[["feel",0],["control",3],["atmosphere",2],["passion",6],["heart",0],["state",3],["character",2],["desire",6],["life",0]],"en":"The old teacher had a quiet spirit that filled the room. She never tried to control us; she only wanted us to feel the life inside the words. The atmosphere in her class was warm, and her own passion for the subject was clear to everyone. She would speak from the heart about a poem, and the whole state of the room would change. I think her character showed in small things. She had a real desire that we should read on our own, and most of us did. Years later I still hear her voice.","zh":"那位老教师有种安静的精神，把整个教室都填满了。她从不试图管住我们，只想让我们感受到字句里的生命。她课上的气氛是暖的，她对这门课的痴迷谁都看得出来。她讲一首诗时会掏心掏肺，整个教室的状态都会变。我觉得她的品格体现在小事上。她真心希望我们自己去找书读，我们大多也这么做了。多年以后，我还能听见她的声音。"},"split":{"tw":[["break",0],["blow",3],["bottle",2],["rent",0],["lot",3],["move",2],["tear",0]],"en":"My brother and I had to split the cost of the rent each month, and we kept a lot of small notes in a bottle on the shelf. One evening an argument over money gave the evening a hard blow. He said the flat was too small and he wanted to move out. I did not want to break with him over such a thing, but a fine tear had opened in the wall, and it seemed to match the one between us. In the end we sat down, and the split of the bill was done in ten quiet minutes.","zh":"我和哥哥每月要分摊房租，我们把一堆零钱收在架上的瓶子里。有天晚上为钱吵了一架，把那个晚上弄得很糟。他说这房子太小，他想搬出去。我不想为这种事跟他闹翻，可墙上裂开了一道细缝，像是跟我们之间的那道对上了。最后我们坐下来，十分钟就把账分好了，安安静静。"},"spoil":{"tw":[["blow",0],["load",3],["treat",2],["squander",6],["cross",0],["ruin",3],["damage",2],["hurry",6],["frustrate",0]],"en":"The rain could spoil the whole trip, and my father did not want to squander his one free week. He would cross the yard a dozen times, checking the load on the roof of the car. A heavy blow of wind had already pulled the cover loose, and there was some damage to the tent. He said we should not hurry, because a small mistake could frustrate the plan and ruin the food. To treat us, he bought cakes at the last shop. The milk would spoil if we left it out, so we packed it deep in the bag.","zh":"这场雨能把整趟旅行毁了，爸爸不想白费他仅有的一周假。他在院子里来回跑了十来趟，检查车顶上捆的行李。一阵大风已经把篷布吹松了，帐篷也有点损坏。他说别急，一个小差错就能让计划泡汤，把吃的也糟蹋了。为了犒劳我们，他在最后一家店买了蛋糕。牛奶放在外面会坏，我们就把它塞进包的最里头。"},"stamp":{"tw":[["boss",0],["date",3],["class",2],["coin",6],["cast",0],["block",3],["die",2],["gift",6],["seal",3]],"en":"At the post office my mother asked for a stamp, then took a coin from her purse. The clerk pressed a date on the envelope with a small die and added a wax seal. A cast of the old sign hung on the wall above the counter. The boss of the shop came out to help when a line of people began to block the door. I wanted to send a small gift to a friend in another class, and I had to hurry before the last post. The whole thing took ten minutes.","zh":"在邮局，妈妈要了一张邮票，又从钱包里掏出一枚硬币。邮递员用小印章在信封上盖了日期，又加了一枚火漆印。柜台上面的墙上挂着一块老招牌的铸件。队伍堵住门口时，店老板出来帮忙。我想寄个小礼物给另一个班的朋友，得赶在最后一班邮车前。前后不过十分钟。"},"stream":{"tw":[["current",0],["river",3],["course",2],["flow",0],["branch",3],["rain",2],["upstream",6],["pour",0]],"en":"A narrow stream runs behind the house and joins the river half a mile away. Its current is weak in summer, when the flow slows to a trickle, and the course of the water changes after every heavy rain. My sister likes to walk upstream along the bank and watch a small branch float past. In winter the stream can pour over the stones and fill the low field. I used to stand there for hours, listening. It was the quietest place I knew. Even now I go back when I need to think.","zh":"一条窄窄的小溪从屋后流过，在半英里外汇入大河。夏天水流很弱，细得只剩一线，每场大雨之后，水的走向都会变。妹妹喜欢沿着岸往上游走，看一根小树枝漂过去。冬天小溪会漫过石头，淹了低处的田。我从前常在那儿一站就是几个钟头，听着水声。那是我知道的最安静的地方。到现在，需要静一静的时候我还会回去。"},"strength":{"tw":[["force",0],["energy",3],["power",2],["strong",6],["posture",0],["momentum",3],["magnitude",2],["balance",6],["potency",0]],"en":"It takes real strength to carry a heavy box up three floors, and my neighbour did it without a word. She is not tall, but she is strong. She keeps her power in her legs, not her arms, and her posture is always straight. At the top she stopped to catch her energy, and I could see the magnitude of the job on her face. The force of the effort left her hands shaking. She said balance matters more than speed. There was a kind of quiet potency in the way she worked, and the momentum of each step never failed.","zh":"把一个沉箱子搬上三楼，真得有力气，邻居却一声不吭就搬上去了。她个子不高，可很结实。她的劲儿在腿上，不在胳膊上，站姿也一直挺直。到了楼上，她停下来缓气，我看得出这活儿有多重。使劲之后她的手都在抖。她说平衡比速度要紧。她干活时有股不声张的劲道，每一步的势头都没断过。"},"stress":{"tw":[["try",0],["rack",3],["express",2],["pain",6],["accent",0],["underscore",3],["force",2],["fatigue",6],["emphasis",2]],"en":"The stress of the exam week showed in her face. She would try to smile, but the fatigue was clear, and she had to put a hand on the rack to steady herself. Her teacher would put the emphasis on one word, and her accent made the stress fall in the wrong place, which added to the pain of learning. He told her to express herself slowly and to underscore the main point. She said the force of the whole year pressed on her at once. By Friday she had stopped trying to hide it.","zh":"考试周的压力写在她脸上。她想笑一笑，可疲惫藏不住，还得用手扶着架子站稳。老师会把重音落在一个词上，而她的口音让重音放错了地方，学起来更费劲。他让她慢慢表达，把要点强调出来。她说，一整年的压力一下子全压过来了。到周五，她已经不再装作没事了。"},"string":{"tw":[["draw",0],["wire",3],["add",2],["minor",6],["train",0],["extension",3],["arrange",2],["series",6],["chain",0]],"en":"A long string of lights hung across the yard, and my father had to add one more wire to reach the last post. He would draw the line tight and then arrange each small bulb in a series along the chain. The train of ideas in his head was simple: one string, one switch, no fuss. A minor fault in the extension cord made the whole row go dark. He fixed it in a minute. When the lights came on, the children stood under them and did not move. It was the best evening of that winter.","zh":"一串长长的彩灯挂在院子上空，爸爸还得再接一根线才够到最后一根柱子。他会把线拉紧，再把每个小灯泡沿着一根链条排成一列。他脑子里的那串念头很简单：一根线、一个开关、不折腾。延长线上有个小毛病，整排灯就黑了。他一分钟就修好了。灯亮起来时，孩子们站在底下，一动不动。那是那个冬天最好的一个晚上。"},"strip":{"tw":[["clean",3],["lead",3],["clear",2],["border",6],["slip",0],["skin",3],["milk",2],["block",6],["bare",0]],"en":"He had to strip the old wire before he could join it to the new one. With a small tool he took off a thin strip of skin from the end, then wiped the copper clean. A bare strip of land ran along the border of the field, where a path led down to the road. My father would slip a strip of tape over the joint to keep the wet out. He asked me for a glass of milk and told me to clear the table. A block of wood held the wire in place. Then we stood back and waited for the light to come on.","zh":"他得先把旧线剥开，才能接到新的上面。他用小工具从线头割下一条薄皮，再把铜芯擦干净。田边一条光秃秃的窄地带，有条小路通向下面的大路。爸爸会往接头上缠一条胶带防潮。他让我倒杯牛奶，又叫我把桌子收拾干净。一块木头把线固定住。然后我们退后站着，等灯亮。"},"stroke":{"tw":[["throw",0],["beat",3],["mark",2],["leg",6],["slash",0],["blow",3],["strike",2],["wound",6],["diagonal",0]],"en":"My grandfather had a stroke in the winter, and for a while he could not lift his left leg. The doctor said the wound inside was small but the effect was large. He would try to beat the weakness every day, and each small mark on his chart showed a little progress. Once he tried to throw a ball and it fell short. Then, with a quick slash of the pen, he drew a diagonal line and smiled. A light blow on the back, a kind word, a slow walk: that was his medicine. He would strike the floor with his stick and keep going.","zh":"爷爷冬天中了一次风，有一阵子连左腿都抬不起来。医生说里头的伤不大，影响却不小。他天天都想把那点虚弱压下去，图上的每一个小记号都表示一点进步。有回他想扔球，球却没扔远。后来他笔尖一划，画了条斜线，笑了。在背上轻拍一下，一句好话，慢慢走上几步，这就是他的药。他总用拐杖敲敲地板，接着往前走。"},"struggle":{"tw":[["fight",3],["box",3],["climb",2],["midst",6],["skin",0],["settle",3],["try",2],["overcome",6],["battle",3]],"en":"The first months in the new country were a hard struggle for my aunt. She had to fight for every small thing, from a box to sit on to a place at the school. Each morning she would climb four floors and try to smile at the door. In the midst of all that, she never lost her skin, as she said, meaning her pride. She wanted to overcome the language, and it was a long battle. Slowly she began to settle, and the days grew easier. I still think of her when I meet someone new here.","zh":"刚到这个国家的头几个月，对姑姑来说是场硬仗。她什么都得争，从一只坐的箱子，到学校里的一个名额。每天早上她都要爬上四楼，在门口努力挤出个笑。在这一堆难处当中，用她的话说，她从没丢掉自己的皮，也就是那点自尊。她想把语言这关攻下来，那是场漫长的仗。后来她慢慢安顿下来，日子才好过些。在这儿每遇到新来的人，我都会想起她。"},"supply":{"tw":[["add",0],["bed",3],["state",2],["demand",1],["fuel",6],["issue",0],["date",3],["bulk",6],["provide",0]],"en":"The village keeps a large supply of water and fuel for the winter. Each family has to add a share, and the state sends a truck when the demand is high. The old store room has a bed in one corner, where the guard sleeps by the bulk of the sacks. The issue is not money but time: the truck comes on a fixed date, and if the road is closed, nobody can provide more. Last year the supply held out, and we did not go cold. That winter the snow was deep, but the lamps stayed lit.","zh":"村里为过冬存着大量水和燃料。每家都得出上一份，需求大的时候，上面会派卡车来。旧库房一角有张床，看守就睡在大堆口袋旁边。问题不在钱，而在时间：卡车按固定日子来，路一断，谁也补不上货。去年存货够用，我们没挨冻。那个冬天雪很深，可灯一直亮着。"},"surround":{"tw":[["ring",0],["medium",3],["cover",2],["stereo",6],["wall",0],["enclose",3],["touch",2],["flash",6],["environment",0]],"en":"Tall trees surround the small house on three sides, and a low stone wall runs along the road. My father used a ring of bricks to enclose the garden and keep the wind out. Inside, the rooms are small, and the thick walls cover every sound from outside. He kept an old stereo in the corner, and music was his whole environment. He would touch the flowers by the path and ask me to look at the light. Once a flash of lightning lit the whole yard, and for a moment the trees seemed to move. The garden was his medium, he said, the way a page is for a writer.","zh":"高高的树从小屋三面把它围住，路边还有一道矮石墙。爸爸用一圈砖把园子围起来挡风。屋里的房间很小，厚墙把外面的声音全挡掉了。屋角放着台旧音响，音乐就是他的整个环境。他会摸摸路边的话，叫我看看光。有次一道闪电把整个院子照亮，一瞬间树好像都动了。他说，这园子就是他的材料，就像纸之于写作者。"},"swallow":{"tw":[["accept",0],["bolt",3],["talk",2],["bite",6],["drink",0],["sip",3],["taste",2],["suck",6],["withdraw",0]],"en":"A swallow sat on the wire above the gate and watched us eat. My father had to swallow his tea in a hurry, then take a quick bite of bread. He would drink from the cup in small sips, but that morning there was no time. The soup had a strange taste, and he could not accept it, so he let it cool. He began to talk about the birds, and how they would withdraw to the south before the cold. I tried to suck the last drop from my spoon. A bolt of wind shook the wire, and the bird was gone.","zh":"一只燕子停在门上的电线上，看着我们吃饭。爸爸只好匆匆把茶咽下去，又赶紧咬了口面包。他平时都是小口小口地喝，可那天早上没工夫。汤味道有点怪，他接受不了，就放着让它凉。他开始说起这些鸟，说天冷之前它们会往南撤。我想把勺子上最后一滴吸干净。一阵风猛地晃了晃电线，鸟就不见了。"},"sweep":{"tw":[["cross",0],["rake",3],["clean",2],["round",6],["sail",0],["swan",3],["cover",2],["straight",6],["brush",0]],"en":"Every Saturday my mother would sweep the yard with a long brush. She liked to rake the leaves into one pile and then cover them with a cloth. A swan sometimes crossed the far end of the lake, and a small sail moved straight across the water. When she was done, the ground looked clean, and she would walk a slow round of the garden to check her work. I used to stand at the gate and watch. It took her an hour, and she never hurried. The yard always smelled of cut grass after that.","zh":"每个星期六，妈妈都用一把长扫帚扫院子。她喜欢把落叶耙成一堆，再用布盖上。湖的那头有时游过一只天鹅，一面小帆直直地划过水面。干完活儿，地上干干净净，她会绕着园子慢慢走一圈，检查一遍。我从前常站在门口看。这要花她一个钟头，她从不着急。之后院子里总有一股青草味。"},"swing":{"tw":[["cut",0],["drive",3],["blow",2],["slow",6],["drop",0],["approach",3],["change",2],["fast",6],["sweep",0]],"en":"The gate began to swing open in the wind, and a slow blow of air moved the curtain inside. My father would drop his bag and drive the car into the yard, then cut the engine. From the window I could watch the approach of a storm as the sky began to change. The old swing in the garden was tied to a tree, and it would move fast when the gusts came. A broom stood by the door to sweep the step. Everything in that house seemed to move with the weather.","zh":"大门被风吹得开始晃动，慢慢敞开，一股气流把屋里的窗帘也吹动了。爸爸会扔下包，把车开进院子，熄了火。从窗口我能看着一场风雨逼近，天色一点点变。园子里那架旧秋千系在树上，风一来就晃得飞快。门口立着一把扫帚，用来扫台阶。那屋里的一切好像都跟着天气动。"},"switch":{"tw":[["change",2],["back",3],["control",2],["allow",6],["throw",0],["break",3],["engage",2],["use",6],["exchange",2]],"en":"The switch on the wall had stopped working, so the light would not come on. My uncle did not allow anyone to use the old one, and he wanted to exchange it for a new part. He had to throw the main control down first to be safe. Then he would break the seal and engage the small metal arm inside. It was a simple change, but he took his time. When he put the cover back, the room filled with light, and he said nothing at all. It was his way, and I learned to wait.","zh":"墙上的开关坏了，灯点不亮。叔叔不许任何人用旧的，他想换一个新零件。为了安全，他得先把总闸推下来。然后他拆开封条，把里面那个小金属臂卡上。这只是个小改动，可他不慌不忙。把盖子装回去，屋里就亮了，他什么也没说。他一向如此，我也学会了等。"},"tap":{"tw":[["knock",0],["milk",3],["blow",2],["stream",6],["strike",0],["lobby",3],["cut",2],["help",6],["beg",0]],"en":"I heard a light tap on the door while I was in the lobby of the small hotel. A woman stood there with a bottle of milk and asked for help with the tap in her room. A thin stream of water came from it, and she had to beg the manager for a new part. He would knock on my door later to say it was done. I offered to cut a piece of rubber and strike it into place with the handle of a spoon. She said it was a small blow, nothing more, and thanked me twice.","zh":"我在小旅馆前厅的时候，听见门上轻轻敲了一下。一个妇人站在那儿，手里拿着瓶牛奶，请我帮她修屋里的水龙头。水从龙头细细地漏出来，她只好去央求经理换个新零件。经理后来敲我的门，说修好了。我说可以割一块橡胶，用勺子柄把它敲进去。她说这是小事一桩，算不了什么，还谢了我两次。"},"tease":{"tw":[["card",0],["kid",3],["woman",2],["giggle",6],["ride",0],["jeer",3],["separate",2],["laugh",6],["bug",0]],"en":"At the school gate the older boys liked to tease the younger ones, and a woman who worked there would walk over and separate them. They would giggle and run, then come back for a ride on the cart. One of them hid a small bug in a card and left it on a desk, which made the whole class laugh. The teacher did not jeer at them; she only asked what they thought was funny. By the end of the week the kid who had started it said sorry, and nobody teased anyone again.","zh":"在校门口，大点的男孩爱拿小的寻开心，那儿做事的一位女士会走过去把他们分开。他们会咯咯笑着跑开，过会儿又回来坐小车兜一圈。其中一个把只小虫藏在卡片里，放在桌上，惹得全班大笑。老师没有嘲笑他们，只问他们觉得哪儿好笑。到周末，那个领头的小孩道了歉，再没人去逗谁了。"},"ticket":{"tw":[["fine",0],["pass",3],["book",2],["lottery",6],["tag",0],["transfer",3],["list",2],["slot",6],["slate",0]],"en":"At the station I had to buy a ticket and book a seat for the night train. The clerk asked me to pass my card through a small slot, then printed a tag with my name and put it on the list. She said I could transfer to another line if I missed the first one. There was a lottery poster on the wall, and a slate board with the times. If I lost the paper, the fine would be heavy, so I put it deep in my pocket. The train left on time, for once.","zh":"在车站，我得买张票，再给夜车订个座位。售票员让我把卡塞进一个小槽里，然后打出一张写着名字的标签，挂到名单上。她说要是误了第一趟，我可以换到另一条线。墙上贴着一张彩票海报，还有块石板写着时刻。要是把票弄丢了，罚款很重，我就把它塞进了口袋深处。这一回，火车准点开了。"},"tip":{"tw":[["lead",0],["head",3],["end",2],["mouth",6],["top",0],["list",3],["mark",2],["finger",6],["wind",0]],"en":"At the very top of the hill the path came to a narrow tip, and from there we could see the whole valley. My uncle put a finger to his mouth and pointed at a bird on the highest branch. He had a tip for walkers: keep your head down on the climb and do not fight the wind. At the far end of the ridge a stone marked the border, and his name was on a list of those who had built the path. I made a small mark in my notebook. It was a fine lead to the day.","zh":"在山的最顶上，小路收成一道窄窄的尖，从那儿能望见整条山谷。叔叔把一根手指放到嘴边，指向最高树枝上的一只鸟。他给走路人出了个主意：上坡时低着头，别跟风较劲。山脊那头有块石头标着界，他的名字还在修路人的名单上。我在本子上画了个小记号。这一天的开头真不错。"},"tool":{"tw":[["instrument",0],["punch",3],["drive",2],["technology",6],["shaft",0],["tap",3],["ride",2],["use",6]],"en":"A good tool can last a lifetime if you treat it well. My grandfather kept a punch, an old instrument for making holes, on the shelf beside a long wooden shaft. He would use it to drive a nail into a plank, then tap the head flat with a hammer. New technology had brought better machines to the shop, but he did not trust them. Once he let me ride the cart to the yard and carry the box back. It was heavy work, and I was proud of it.","zh":"一件好工具只要爱惜，能用一辈子。爷爷架子上放着一个打孔器，一个打眼用的老家伙，旁边靠着一根长木柄。他拿它把钉子敲进木板，再用锤子把钉头敲平。新技术给铺子带来了更好的机器，可他信不过。有一回他让我坐上小车去院子，把那箱子搬回来。那活儿不轻，我干得挺得意。"},"toy":{"tw":[["play",0],["slide",3],["act",2],["shoe",6],["fiddle",0],["balloon",3],["dog",2],["candy",6],["miniature",0]],"en":"The child left a small toy under the bed, a tiny miniature car with one wheel missing. She would play with it for hours, making it slide across the floor while the dog slept beside her. Her brother liked to fiddle with a balloon until it burst, which made her act as if nothing had happened. A single shoe lay by the door, and a paper of candy sat by the chair. Their mother said the flat was full of small things. It was, and it was never quiet. I liked being there anyway.","zh":"孩子把一个小玩具落在床底下，一辆迷你小汽车，少了一个轮子。她能玩上几个钟头，让它在地板上滑来滑去，狗就在旁边睡着。她弟弟爱摆弄气球，非要弄爆不可，她就装作什么都没发生。门口丢着一只鞋，椅子边搁着一包糖。他们的妈妈说，家里到处都是小东西。确实如此，而且从没安静过。我却喜欢待在那儿。"},"trace":{"tw":[["draw",0],["write",3],["mark",2],["identify",6],["follow",0],["construct",3],["read",2],["contain",6],["hunt",0]],"en":"The ground was wet, and it was easy to follow the trace of a small animal. My father would draw a line in the mud with a stick and try to identify the print. He could read a track the way other people read a book. There was no mark to show where it had gone, so we had to hunt along the fence. He told me that a good story should contain only the facts you can see. Then he began to construct a small trap with wire, though we never used it. Later I would write the whole day down in a small book.","zh":"地面是湿的，跟着一只小动物的踪迹走很容易。爸爸会用树枝在泥里画一道线，猜那是什么脚印。他读踪迹，就像别人读书一样。地上没有记号指出它去了哪儿，我们只好顺着篱笆找。他说，好故事里只该有你看得见的事实。后来他用铁丝做了个小套子，虽然我们一次也没用上。再晚些，我把这一天都写进了一个小本子。"},"trade":{"tw":[["deal",3],["close",3],["business",2],["export",6],["sell",2],["market",3],["class",2],["exchange",6],["switch",0]],"en":"My uncle runs a small trade in second-hand tools. Every morning he opens his market stall and tries to close a good deal before the sun gets high. It is not a large business, and he will sell almost anything, from a lamp to a box of nails. He learned the trade from his father, who used to export cloth. Once a customer wanted to switch an old watch for a knife, and they made the exchange with a handshake. He serves every class of customer, and they all come back.","zh":"叔叔做的是旧工具的买卖，摊子不大。每天早晨他支起摊位，趁太阳还不高的时候尽量把一笔生意谈成。这生意规模不大，他什么都卖，从一盏灯到一盒钉子。这行当是他跟父亲学的，他父亲从前出口布匹。有回一个顾客想用旧手表换把刀，两人握个手就换了。什么样的客人都接待，而这些人还都成了回头客。"},"transfer":{"tw":[["change",0],["bring",3],["move",2],["allow",6],["channel",0],["carry",3],["travel",2],["option",6],["remove",0]],"en":"My father had to transfer his old files to a new computer before the office closed. It was slow work, and he had to change the settings first. He would bring one folder at a time and move it across with a small tool, then carry the rest on a drive. Some files came through a different channel and did not allow a clean copy. He said there was one more option: remove the drive and start again. It took four hours, and he did not travel home until dark.","zh":"办公室关门前，爸爸得把旧文件转到新电脑上。这活儿很慢，他还得先改设置。他一次带一个文件夹过去，用小工具移一下，剩下的拷到盘上搬走。有些文件走的是另一条通道，没法完整复制。他说还有个办法：把盘拔了重来。前后花了四个钟头，他到家时天都黑了。"},"trap":{"tw":[["hole",0],["web",3],["hold",2],["escape",6],["pin",0],["net",3],["mouth",2],["shoot",6],["ambush",0]],"en":"In the corner of the garden there was a small trap for mice, a box with a hole and a metal net. My grandmother would pin a piece of cheese inside and wait. A spider had built a web above it, and the flies could not escape. Once a bird came too close and tried to shoot up into the air, but the net would not hold it. She let it go at once. After that she said she had no wish to ambush any living thing, and she left the trap open at the mouth.","zh":"园子角落里有个逮老鼠的小套子，一个带窟窿的箱子，蒙着铁网。奶奶会往里面别一块奶酪，然后等着。箱子上面有蜘蛛结了网，苍蝇都逃不掉。有一回一只鸟靠得太近，想蹿上天，可网没困住它。她立刻把它放了。从那以后她说，她不想再暗算任何活物，就把那套子的口一直敞着。"},"tune":{"tw":[["air",0],["service",3],["pitch",2],["song",6],["line",0],["theme",3],["adjust",2],["pop",6],["strain",0]],"en":"My father would hum a tune while he worked, a simple air without words. He could not read music, but he could hold a line and keep the pitch true. At the shop the radio played the same pop song all day, and by evening the theme was stuck in my head. He would adjust the old set when the signal began to strain. On Sundays the service at the small church had a slow song that everyone knew. He said music was the best way to change the air in a room.","zh":"爸爸干活时总爱哼个小调，一段没有词的简单旋律。他不识谱，可他能把一条音线拿住，音准也稳。铺子里的收音机整天放着同一首流行歌，到晚上那个调子就在我脑子里转不出去。信号一紧，他就去调那台旧机子。星期天小教堂的礼拜上有一首慢歌，人人都会唱。他说，音乐是换一换屋里空气的最好办法。"},"upset":{"tw":[["trouble",0],["pain",3],["move",2],["beat",6],["disturb",0],["embarrass",3],["shape",2],["win",6],["disorder",0]],"en":"She looked upset after the letter came, and she did not want to talk. The news was a trouble she had carried for years, and it brought back an old pain. Her hands would move over the table as if she were looking for something. My brother tried to beat her at cards that evening to cheer her up, but it only seemed to disturb her more. I did not want to embarrass her, so I said nothing. In the end she went out, and the shape of the room felt empty. The whole house was in a quiet disorder. Nobody could win that night.","zh":"信来了以后，她一脸心烦，什么也不想说。那消息是她扛了多年的一件麻烦，又把旧痛翻了出来。她的手在桌上摸来摸去，像在找什么东西。晚上弟弟想打牌赢她几局逗她开心，结果好像只让她更不安。我不想让她难堪，就什么也没说。最后她出去了，屋子空落落的。整个家都乱得悄无声息。那天晚上谁也没赢。"},"value":{"tw":[["rate",3],["price",3],["see",2],["share",6],["appreciate",0],["admire",3],["worth",2],["account",6],["measure",2]],"en":"The old painting on the wall had little value for anyone but us. Its price in the market was small, and a dealer gave it a low rate. But my mother would see in it the face of her own grandmother, and she would sit and admire it for a long time. We all share that feeling, and we appreciate what it means. She said the true worth of a thing cannot be measured with a ruler, and it has no place in any account. To her it was priceless. She would dust it every Sunday and never move it.","zh":"墙上那幅旧画，除了我们，谁看都不值钱。它在市场上价钱很低，一个画商给的估价也不高。可妈妈能从里面看见她自己奶奶的脸，她会坐着看上很久。我们都有同感，也珍惜它的意思。她说，一样东西真正的价值没法用尺子量，账上也写不进去。对她来说，它是无价的。每个星期天她都擦一擦它，从不挪动。"},"weed":{"tw":[["grass",0],["stub",3],["band",2],["manure",6],["pot",0],["nettle",3],["remove",2],["bully",6],["smoke",0]],"en":"The garden was full of weed, and my grandfather spent every morning pulling it out. He would remove each nettle with a thick glove, then drop it in a band of light by the wall. The grass grew tall around the pots, and he would cut the stub of an old root with a knife. Smoke rose from a small fire at the back, and the smell of manure hung over the beds. He said a weed is only a plant in the wrong place, and that people should not bully it for that.","zh":"园子里全是杂草，爷爷每天早上都在拔。他会戴着厚手套把每一棵荨麻拔掉，扔到墙边一条光带里。花盆周围的草长得很高，他会用刀把一截老根剁掉。后面小火烧着，冒起烟来，粪肥的气味罩在菜畦上。他说，杂草不过是长错地方的植物，人不能因为这个就欺负它。"},"whip":{"tw":[["strap",3],["cat",3],["beat",2],["caucus",6],["lash",0],["switch",3],["blow",2],["party",6],["slash",0]],"en":"My grandfather made whips and straps for the men who drove carts. He would lash a long line of leather to a handle and beat it flat with a wooden tool, then slash off the rough edge. A thin switch from a young tree could serve the same purpose. Once a small cat slept by the bench and woke at every blow of his hand. In the yard a party of drivers gathered, almost a little caucus, and each of them took one home. He never used a whip on an animal himself.","zh":"爷爷给赶车的人做鞭子和皮带。他会把一条长皮带缠到手柄上，用木工具敲平，再把毛边削掉。一根小树上削下来的细枝条也能当同样的用。有一回一只小猫睡在长凳边，他每敲一下它就醒。院子里聚了一群车夫，简直像开个小会，每人拿了一条回去。他自己从没用鞭子打过牲口。"},"wing":{"tw":[["fly",0],["flight",3],["position",2],["front",6],["extension",0],["buzz",3],["stage",2],["radical",6],["flank",0]],"en":"A bird with a hurt wing could not fly, and it sat on the front step for two days. My mother made a small extension to the box and put it there, away from the cat. She would buzz around the kitchen, and then stop to check its position. On the stage of the old hall a play was being prepared, and the young director had a radical idea: no one would move. I watched the bird from the flank of the door, and I hoped its first flight would be a good one.","zh":"一只伤了一边翅膀的鸟飞不起来，在门口台阶上待了两天。妈妈给那个箱子加了个小延伸的窝，把它放在那儿，离猫远些。她在厨房里忙得团团转，又停下来看看它的位置。老礼堂的台上在排一出戏，年轻的导演有个大胆的主意：谁都不许动。我站在门侧看着那只鸟，盼着它头一次飞能飞好。"},"witness":{"tw":[["find",0],["catch",3],["experience",2],["evidence",6],["see",0],["spy",3],["watch",2],["suspect",6],["spectator",0]],"en":"From the window I was the only witness to what happened in the lane. I could see a man run past and catch a bag from someone's hand. It was not my experience to watch such a thing, and my heart beat fast. I looked for evidence, but the ground was dry and left no mark. The police could not find the bag anywhere. A neighbour said she would spy on the street from her own door. Later they asked me to describe the suspect, and I said he was thin and quick. I was only a spectator, but my words counted.","zh":"从窗口看过去，我是巷子里那件事唯一的目击者。我看见一个男人跑过去，从别人手里抢走一个包。我从来没经历过这样的事，心跳得厉害。我想找点证据，可地是干的，什么痕迹也没留下。警察哪儿都没找到那个包。邻居说她会从自己门口盯着街上。后来他们让我描述那个嫌疑人，我说他又瘦又快。我只是个旁观的人，可我的话也算数。"},"wound":{"tw":[["hurt",2],["cut",3],["damage",2],["shoulder",6],["injure",0],["pull",3],["arouse",2],["neck",6],["bruise",0]],"en":"The doctor cleaned the wound on my shoulder and put on a cloth. I had cut my arm on a nail, and the pull of the heavy box had made it worse. She said the damage was small, but a deep bruise would stay for a week. I did not want to injure it again, so I kept still. Her voice was calm, and it did not arouse any fear in me. She turned my neck gently to check the muscle. In a few days the hurt was nearly gone. I still have a thin line there.","zh":"医生给我肩上的伤口做了清理，又敷上一块布。我胳膊被钉子划破了，搬重箱子一使劲，伤得更重。她说伤不严重，但淤青要留一个星期。我不想再弄伤它，就老实待着。她说话很平静，一点没让我害怕。她轻轻转过我的脖子，查看肌肉。几天后疼就差不多没了。那儿至今还留着一道细线。"},"wrap":{"tw":[["roll",0],["ball",3],["cover",2],["cake",6],["wind",0],["film",3],["move",2],["nail",6],["enclose",0]],"en":"Before the party my sister had to wrap a small cake for our aunt. She would roll the paper around it and cover the top with a ribbon, then move it into a box. A ball of string sat on the table, and she used a thin film to keep the cake fresh. She had to nail the lid shut with two small pins. Outside the wind began to rise, so I helped her carry the parcel to the car. She said she would enclose a short letter as well.","zh":"聚会前，姐姐得把一个小蛋糕包好送给姑姑。她把纸卷着裹上去，顶上再系条带子，然后放进盒子。桌上搁着一团线绳，她还用一层薄膜给蛋糕保鲜。盒盖得用两根小钉钉住。外面起风了，我帮她把包裹搬到车上。她说还要附上一封短信。"},"season":{"tw":[["seasoning",4],["flavour",0],["fall",3],["game",6],["temper",0],["spring",3],["league",6]],"en":"Every season brought a new dish to our kitchen. In spring my mother would pick the first herbs, and their flavour went into a light soup with almost no seasoning. In fall the game from the woods needed a slow fire, and she had to watch her temper when the oven was late. My father followed the local league on the small radio and would not move until the match ended. Winter came, and we ate the last jars from the shelf. Nothing on that table ever came from far away. I cook this way still, and let the seasons set the menu.","zh":"每个季节都会给我们的厨房添一道新菜。春天妈妈去采第一批香草，那份鲜味放进清汤里，几乎不用什么调料。秋天林子里的野味得用小火慢慢炖，烤炉晚了，她就得压住脾气。爸爸守着那台小收音机听本地的联赛，比赛不结束他是不动的。冬天来了，我们吃架子上最后几罐存货。那张桌上的东西，从来没有一样是从远处来的。我到今天还这么做饭，菜单由季节来定。"},"role":{"tw":[["office",0],["heavy",3],["duty",2],["life",6],["use",0],["position",3],["utility",2],["function",0]],"en":"My sister had a small role in the village play, and she took it more seriously than anyone in the office would have believed. Her duty was to open the second act, which sounds easy but carries a heavy weight when the hall is full. She would stand in her position behind the curtain and wait for her cue. In real life she is quiet, and she finds little use for the stage tricks others enjoy. Still, her function in the play was clear: without that first line, nothing else worked. I think she liked the utility of it. On the last night she did not miss a word.","zh":"我妹妹在村里的戏里演一个小角色，她认真得办公室里谁都不会信。她的任务是开第二幕，听着容易，可满场的时候，这一句分量很重。她会站在幕布后自己的位子上，等她的提示。生活里她话很少，别人爱玩的那套舞台花招，她也不怎么用得上。不过她在这个戏里的功能很清楚：没有那一句，后面都不成立。我想她喜欢的就是这种用处。最后一场她一个字都没漏。"},"rot":{"tw":[["waste",0],["hang",3],["decay",2],["rust",6],["bunk",0],["devolve",2],["wither",6],["decompose",0]],"en":"The old barn had been left to rot for twenty years, and the roof had begun to decay in the middle. A metal hook was still hanging from a beam, eaten by rust, and the wooden bunk in the corner had almost fallen apart. In summer the smell of things left to decompose filled the whole field, and the walls seemed to wither and lean. My uncle called it a waste of good timber, and he said the place had begun to devolve into a heap of sticks. We cleared the bunk and hung a new door on it that autumn.","zh":"那座旧谷仓就那么烂了二十年，屋顶中间已经开始朽坏。横梁上还挂着一个铁钩，锈得不成样子；角落里的木床铺几乎散了架。夏天，那些任由腐烂的东西发出的气味弥漫整片田野，墙也像是枯瘦了，往外斜。我叔叔说这是白白糟蹋了好木料，还说这地方正一点点败落成一堆木棍。那年秋天我们清了那张床铺，给它装上了一扇新门。"},"scale":{"tw":[["plate",0],["balance",3],["bit",2],["impact",6],["shell",0],["index",3],["climb",2],["significant",6]],"en":"The old man at the market had a scale with a brass plate, and he would set it on the shelf and balance it with a tiny bit of lead. He said the numbers on the index had to line up before anything was sold. A broken shell lay beside the weights, and it made a small impact every time he moved the tray. The climb in prices that year was significant, and he felt it on every sack. Still, he would not raise his own prices by a single coin. That is why people walked past three other stalls to reach him.","zh":"集市上那位老人有一杆秤，秤盘是黄铜的，他会把它放在架子上，用一丁点铅配平。他说，刻度上的数对不上就不卖。砝码旁边摆着一只破贝壳，他每挪一次托盘，它就磕出一点小动静。那一年物价涨得厉害，他每一袋都能感觉到。可他自己的价钱，一个铜板也不肯加。就为这个，人们宁可走过另外三个摊子，也要到他这儿来。"},"scene":{"tw":[["fit",0],["light",3],["situation",2],["footage",6],["picture",0],["stage",3],["sight",6],["view",0]],"en":"The old theatre was used for one night as a film set. A young director stood at the back and watched the final scene again and again. The light on the small stage was too dim, and the picture on her screen did not fit the mood she wanted. She checked the footage twice, then called the crew to change the view. For a moment the whole situation felt wrong. Then a man walked into sight from the left, and she knew the shot was ready. Nobody in the room spoke while the camera rolled. She kept that frame in mind for years.","zh":"那座老戏院有一个晚上被当成了片场。一个年轻导演站在后排，把最后一场戏看了一遍又一遍。小舞台上的光太暗，她屏幕上的画面怎么也不合她想要的情绪。她把素材核对了两遍，然后叫剧组换了个视角。有那么一会儿，整个情形都不对了。接着一个男人从左边的画面外围走了进来，她知道这个镜头成了。机器转动的时候屋里没人出声。这个画面她记了很多年。"},"shame":{"tw":[["pity",0],["foul",3],["arouse",2],["utter",6],["disgrace",0],["reproach",3],["insult",6],["dishonour",0]],"en":"They found out in the spring that my uncle had sold the family land and kept the money. It was a disgrace nobody in the village could forget. My grandmother would not utter his name for a year. Whenever someone mentioned him, she would reproach herself instead, as if the shame were hers. His brother sent him one letter, full of insult, and another full of pity. The whole affair seemed to arouse only quiet anger in my father. He said a foul act brings its own dishonour, and no punishment from us can add to it. We never spoke of it again.","zh":"那年春天我们发现，我叔把家里的地卖了，钱自己留下了。这在村里是没人能忘掉的耻辱。奶奶有一整年不肯说出他的名字。谁提起他，她反倒怪自己，好像丢人的是她。他哥哥给他写过一封信，满纸都是辱骂；又写过一封，满纸都是可怜他。整件事在我爸心里似乎只搅起一种安静的怒气。他说，一件下作的事本身就带着羞耻，我们再罚他也添不上什么。后来我们再没提过。"},"shave":{"tw":[["plane",0],["razor",3],["cut",2],["shove",6],["trim",0],["fleece",3],["reduce",2],["twirl",6]],"en":"On Saturday mornings my grandfather would shave the older men of the street in his small back room. He kept a straight razor on a clean cloth and a wooden plane on the shelf beside it, though he never used the plane for wood. First he would trim the hair with slow care, then shove the chair round and twirl it once, as if to show off. He cut almost nothing, yet the shave always felt close. In winter he wore a grey fleece jacket and would reduce the price for anyone with little money. He said a good razor should last a lifetime, and his did.","zh":"每个星期六早上，爷爷都在他那间小里屋里给街上的老人们刮脸。他把一把直剃刀放在干净的布上，旁边的架子上还摆着一把木刨，尽管他从不用它刨木头。他先慢慢地修剪头发，再把椅子推过去转上一圈，像是显摆一下。他几乎没割到过什么，可那胡子总刮得贴面。冬天他穿一件灰色的绒夹克，遇上钱少的人还会少收点。他说一把好剃刀该用一辈子，他那把确实用了很久。"},"shed":{"tw":[["drop",0],["seed",3],["move",2],["stock",6],["throw",0],["pour",2],["hang",6],["cast",0]],"en":"Behind the house stood a small shed where my father kept his tools and a stock of old pots. Every spring he would move the boxes out, hang his coats on a nail, and pour the last of the seed into a tin. Then he would drop a few seeds into each pot, one by one, and throw the empty bags away. He liked to cast a long look at the young plants before he locked the door. One year a neighbour came to help and, with a careless move, knocked the whole shelf down. My father only said the shed had seen worse, and began again.","zh":"屋后有个小棚子，我爸把工具和一堆旧花盆都存在里面。每年春天他都把箱子搬出来，把外套挂在钉子上，把最后一点种子倒进铁罐。然后他一颗一颗把种子点进每个盆里，再把空袋子扔出去。锁门前他喜欢朝那些幼苗长长地看上一眼。有一年邻居来帮忙，一个不小心的动作把整层架子都碰倒了。我爸只说这棚子见过更糟的，又重新收拾起来。"},"shore":{"tw":[["land",0],["strand",3],["hold",2],["inland",6],["prop",0],["bolster",3],["beam",2],["coast",6]],"en":"The little boat came back to the shore just before dark. My uncle had to hold the rope while the waves pushed it in, and the wet strand of it cut his hand. Two men from the coast guard ran down to prop the hull with a beam of wood, then used a second beam to bolster the broken side. Farther inland the lights of the village were already on. He had left that land as a boy and never thought he would return to this same stretch of shore. Now he stood there, salt on his face, and did not want to leave.","zh":"小船天快黑时才回到岸边。浪往里推船，我叔得拽住缆绳，湿透的那股绳磨着他的手。海岸警卫队的两个人跑下来，用一根木梁顶住船身，又用第二根木梁撑住撞破的那一侧。再往内陆看，村里的灯已经亮了。他小时候离开这片土地，从没想过会回到同样这一段海岸。此刻他站在那儿，脸上带着咸味，不想走了。"},"signal":{"tw":[["sign",0],["mark",3],["tell",2],["frequency",6],["indicate",0],["alarm",3],["communicate",2],["pulse",6]],"en":"At the top of the hill stood a tall radio tower, and its only job was to send one signal out across the valley. My aunt worked in the little room below it. She had to mark each message on a chart, note the frequency, and communicate with the boats along the coast. When the pulse of the machine changed, a red light would indicate that something was wrong. There was an alarm that could tell her within seconds. She would reach for the sign above her desk, the one that read stay calm, and wait. Some nights nobody answered her, and she kept sending anyway.","zh":"山顶上立着一座高广播塔，它唯一的活儿就是把一个信号送过整个山谷。我姑在它下面那间小屋里工作。她得把每条消息标在图上，记下频率，再跟沿岸的船只联络。机器脉搏一变，一盏红灯就会显示出了问题。有个警报器能在几秒内告诉她。她会伸手去够桌上方那块牌子，上面写着保持冷静，然后等下去。有些夜里没人回应她，她还是照样一直发。"},"site":{"tw":[["situation",0],["camp",3],["position",2],["web",6],["locate",0],["dig",3],["station",2],["park",6]],"en":"Two summers ago I joined a small team at a dig on the edge of the city. Our site lay behind an old camp that had once held workers from the railway. Every morning we had to locate the right position with a long tape, then mark it before we could dig. The station was close enough to hear, and a park with tall trees lay just beyond the fence. By noon the whole situation changed, because the sun made the ground too hard. We kept a web of notes and small drawings, so that nothing found that day would be lost later.","zh":"两年前的夏天，我加入了城边一个小小发掘队。我们的场地在一片旧营地的后面，那营地曾住过修铁路的工人。每天早上我们都得用长皮尺定位，标好位置才能开挖。车站离得近，听得见动静；篱笆那头就是一座长着高树的公园。到了中午，整个情况就变了，因为太阳把地烤得太硬。我们把笔记和草图理成一张网，这样那天挖到的东西以后就不会丢。"},"smash":{"tw":[["break",2],["blast",3],["blow",2],["rip",6],["hit",2],["return",2],["grab",6],["knock",0]],"en":"A van came too fast round the corner and hit the low wall outside our gate. The blow threw a small stone into the kitchen window and made the glass smash across the floor. My mother ran to grab the boy before he could walk on it. There was a second, softer knock as a piece of the wall fell, then a loud blast as something burst under the van. The driver did not return for an hour. Nothing would break her silence; she only swept the glass into a bag and tied a cloth round a long rip in her coat.","zh":"一辆面包车拐弯太快，撞上了我们门外的矮墙。这一撞把一块小石头甩进厨房窗户，玻璃哗啦一声碎了一地。我妈赶紧把男孩抓开，怕他踩上去。墙掉下一块时又轻轻磕响了一声，接着车底下有什么爆开，发出好大一声炸响。司机一个小时后才回来。她一句话也没说，只把碎玻璃扫进袋子，又在衣上一个长口子上扎了块布。"},"soul":{"tw":[["individual",0],["creature",3],["spirit",2],["love",6],["mortal",0],["ghost",3],["pop",6],["psyche",0]],"en":"Every Friday night my sister would play old pop songs in a small bar near the river. She was a quiet individual off stage, but once she began to sing, something in her spirit opened. People said her love of music could reach the soul of any creature in the room, even the ones who had come only for a drink. She used to say that a mortal has one short life, so sing while you can. Once a man told her he had heard a ghost singing the same tune, and she laughed. She never seemed to study her own psyche; she just sang.","zh":"每个星期五晚上，我姐都会在河边一家小酒吧里唱些老流行歌。下了台她是个安静的人，可一开口，她身上有什么东西就打开了。人们说她对音乐的爱能碰到屋里任何一个生灵的灵魂，连那些只为喝一杯来的人也碰得到。她常说，凡人一辈子很短，能唱就唱。有一次一个男人说，他听见一个鬼魂也在唱同一支曲子，她笑了。她好像从不琢磨自己的心理，只是唱。"},"spell":{"tw":[["piece",0],["snap",3],["mean",2],["play",6],["write",0],["shift",2],["season",6],["charm",0]],"en":"The winter that year was a long cold spell, and work at the factory came in shifts. My father would write one short piece for the local paper each week, and it means a little extra money for us. In the evening my sister and I would play cards while he read his own lines aloud. He had a quiet charm and could make any dull season sound interesting. Once, in the middle of a night shift, the old machine gave a snap and stopped. He did not panic, but sat down and began to spell out a letter to the owner by hand.","zh":"那年冬天是一段很长的寒潮，厂里的活按班次轮着来。我爸每周给本地报纸写一小篇稿子，这笔钱对我们是不小的补贴。晚上他和我们姐弟俩打牌，同时把自己的稿子念出声来。他自有一种安静的魅力，能把任何沉闷的季节说得有意思。有一次上夜班，那台旧机器咔的一声停了。他没慌，坐下来动手给老板写起信来。"},"spin":{"tw":[["twist",2],["centrifuge",3],["drive",2],["fast",6],["reel",0],["present",2],["arm",6],["whirl",0]],"en":"In the school lab a small machine began to spin faster and faster, and the students watched the numbers climb. It was a centrifuge, and their teacher had to present the result to a visiting group that morning. One girl would twist a dial, then step back while the drum began to whirl. There was a long arm of metal holding the lid, and it shook with every turn. The whole thing was too fast to follow by eye. A boy tried to drive the switch with a ruler, and the teacher stopped him. It was like a reel of film running without a picture.","zh":"学校实验室里一台小机器开始转得越来越快，学生们盯着数字往上蹿。那是台离心机，老师那天早上还得把结果讲给一批来访的人听。一个女孩拧一下旋钮，再退后一步，看转筒打转。有一根长长的金属臂压着盖子，每转一圈都跟着抖。整个东西快得眼睛跟不上。一个男孩想用尺子去拨开关，被老师拦住了。它就像一盘没有画面的胶片在空转。"},"staff":{"tw":[["faculty",0],["man",3],["body",2],["personnel",6],["stave",0],["office",3],["force",2],["officer",6]],"en":"The school had a small staff, and every teacher also worked in the main office once a week. The whole faculty met on Friday after lunch, when the office would fill with talk about new pupils. An older man on the teaching body, who had once been an officer in the army, kept a wooden stave by the door for the winter ice. He said the staff of any school was really a force, though nobody used that word. The personnel list had not changed for years. He would stave off every question about money with a quiet joke, and everyone would laugh.","zh":"学校人手不多，每位老师每周还得去主办公室帮一天。午饭后全体教师碰头，办公室里就全是关于新学生的谈话。教师队伍里有个年纪大的男人，当年在部队当过军官，冬天结冰时他总在门边放一根木棍。他说，任何一所学校的全体人员其实都是一种力量，虽然没人用这个词。人员名单好几年没变过。谁问钱的事，他都用一句安静的笑话挡回去，大家都笑。"},"stir":{"tw":[["excite",0],["disgust",3],["move",2],["boil",6],["raise",0],["work",2],["butter",6],["shake",0]],"en":"The kitchen began to stir as soon as my mother turned on the radio. She would raise the lid, let the soup boil, and work the butter into the dough with her hands. The smell could excite anyone who walked in, though the sight of the grey fish on the board might disgust them. She would move between the table and the stove without hurry, tasting as she went. She never measured anything; she worked by the smell and the sound of the pot. When the pot began to shake on the flame, she only turned it down. Years later I still stir a pan the way she did.","zh":"我妈一开收音机，厨房就活了起来。她会掀开锅盖，让汤咕嘟咕嘟地滚，用手把黄油揉进面团。那香味能让谁走进来都兴奋，尽管案板上那条灰鱼的模样也许让人反胃。她在桌子和灶台之间不紧不慢地来回，边走边尝。她从不用量杯，全凭气味和锅里的声音。锅子开始在火上抖动，她只是把火关小。多年以后，我颠勺的样子还是跟她一样。"},"storm":{"tw":[["force",0],["blizzard",3],["act",2],["hurricane",6],["surprise",0],["blow",2],["cyclone",6],["rage",0]],"en":"The storm came in from the sea on a Tuesday and stayed for three days. No one had expected a blizzard so late in the year, and the surprise left the whole town without power. The wind would blow so hard that the old sign above the shop began to rage against its post. People said it was less a cyclone than a slow hurricane that would not move. In such weather the only wise act was to stay inside and let the force of it pass over the roofs. My mother filled every pot with water before the lights went out.","zh":"那场暴风雨星期二从海上过来，一连待了三天。谁也没料到这么晚还会有暴雪，这场意外让整个镇子都断了电。风大得连店上方那块旧招牌都开始跟柱子较劲。人们说它算不上旋风，更像是赖着不走的慢飓风。这种天气里唯一明智的做法就是待在屋里，让那股力量从屋顶上过去。灯灭之前，我妈把每个锅都装满了水。"},"style":{"tw":[["fashion",3],["fit",3],["taste",2],["modern",6],["manner",0],["form",3],["simple",6],["title",0]],"en":"My aunt ran a small shop where she sold clothes in a simple, quiet style. She had a good eye for fashion but no patience for what was merely modern. Each piece had to fit the person, not the picture in a magazine. She would study the form of a coat, the way it hung, and then change the title on the label to something plainer. Her taste was sure, and her manner with customers never changed. She said a good garment should last long enough to go out of style, and then come quietly back again. She never hurried a customer, even on a busy day.","zh":"我姑开了家小店，卖的衣服是一种简单、安静的风格。她对时尚眼光很好，却看不上那些只算时髦的东西。每件衣服都得合人身，而不是合杂志上的图片。她会琢磨一件外套的形，看它垂下来的样子，然后把标签上的名字改成更朴素的。她的品味很稳，待客的举止也从不改变。她说，一件好衣服该活得够久，久到过时了再悄悄回来。再忙的日子，她也从不催客人。"},"swear":{"tw":[["trust",0],["count",3],["express",2],["oath",6],["curse",0],["hold",3],["vow",2],["bless",6]],"en":"Before the old man left the village, he asked us to swear one thing: that we would hold the well in common and never let it dry. He did not want a written paper, only our word. My father gave a vow, my mother blessed the new stone, and the neighbours made an oath together under the tree. The word trust was not used that evening, and no one thought to express it in a speech, but everyone felt it. Later a man who broke the rule earned a loud curse from his own brother. You can count on one hand the days like that one.","zh":"老人离开村子前，要我们发一个誓：这口井归大家共有，绝不让它干。他不要写字的纸，只要一句话。我爸立了誓愿，我妈给那块新石头祝了福，邻居们一起在树下宣了誓。那天晚上没人提到信任这个词，也没人想到要在讲话里表达它，可人人都感觉得到。后来有个破了规矩的人，被自己的哥哥骂得很难听。那样的日子，一只手就数得过来。"},"tense":{"tw":[["strain",0],["past",3],["change",2],["relax",1],["stalemate",6],["present",3],["affect",2],["calm",6]],"en":"The two men sat across the table in a long, tense silence. Their argument had reached a stalemate, and neither side would move. The room was small, and the clock on the wall seemed louder than usual. The strain showed in the way each held his cup. My father, who was trying to keep the present mood calm, said that the past should not be allowed to affect the deal. Then he asked them to relax and have some tea. That small change in the room was enough. Ten minutes later they shook hands, and nobody mentioned the words spoken before.","zh":"两个男人隔着桌子坐着，好一阵紧张的沉默。他们的争论陷入了僵局，谁也不肯动。屋子很小，墙上的钟好像比平时响。那份紧绷从两人端杯子的样子里就看得出来。我爸想让眼前的局面保持平静，说过去的事不该影响这笔生意。然后他请两人放松，喝口茶。屋里这一点小小的变化就够了。十分钟后他们握了手，谁也没提先前说过的话。"},"title":{"tw":[["claim",0],["father",3],["right",2],["final",6],["style",0],["miss",3],["champion",6],["entitle",0]],"en":"My father had one great claim to fame: he was the champion runner of our town for three years. He ran in a plain style, with no show about it, and often won the final race of the season by a step. People said he had a natural right to the title, though he never spoke of it. Once he missed a race because my mother was ill, and he did not complain. He would tell me that a win does not entitle you to anything except the next start. He was the same quiet man the day he stopped running.","zh":"我爸有一件值得夸的事：他连着三年是我们镇的赛跑冠军。他跑起来姿势朴素，没有半点花哨，季节里最后一场常常只赢出一步。人们说这个头衔他当之无愧，可他从不提。有一回我妈病了，他错过一场比赛，也没抱怨。他跟我说，赢一次不能说明什么，只意味着还能有下一次起跑。他不再跑的那天，还是那个安静的人。"},"tour":{"tw":[["spell",0],["visit",3],["travel",2],["stage",6],["circuit",0],["journey",2],["final",6],["hitch",0]],"en":"That spring the small band went on a long tour of the north. For eight weeks they had to travel by night and play on whatever stage a town could give them. The spell of cold weather made the circuit harder, and once a broken wheel left them stuck. Nothing went quite as planned on that long, dusty road. They would visit a new place every few days, and then hitch a lift to the next one. On the final night my sister sang alone in a hall with no seats. She said the whole journey was worth that one song.","zh":"那年春天，这支小乐队去北方做了一趟很长的巡演。八个星期里，他们得夜里赶路，在镇上能给的随便什么台子上演出。一段寒潮让这趟巡回路更难走，有一次车轮坏了，把他们困在路上。那条尘土飞扬的长路上，没有一件事完全按计划走。他们每隔几天到一个新地方，然后再搭车去下一个。最后一晚，我姐在一个没有座位的礼堂里独自唱。她说，那首歌让整趟旅程都值了。"},"twist":{"tw":[["pull",2],["curl",3],["dance",2],["odd",6],["wind",0],["snake",3],["move",2],["bend",0]],"en":"The road up to the old mine had a strange twist near the top, where it seemed to bend back on itself. My uncle liked to pull the car over there and watch a curl of smoke rise from a hut below. An odd wind would come down the valley and make the dry grass move like a slow dance. Once a snake crossed the road and disappeared into the stones. He would wind down the window and just listen. He never told anyone why he liked that spot so much. Sometimes the two of us stayed there for an hour without a word.","zh":"上老矿山的这条路，快到顶时有个奇怪的弯，像是往自己身上折回来。我叔喜欢把车停在那儿，看下面一间小屋升起一缕烟。一阵怪风从山谷下来，把干草吹得像跳一支慢舞。有一次一条蛇横过路面，钻进石头缝里。他会把车窗摇下来，就那样听着。他从不告诉别人，为什么这么喜欢那个地方。有时我们俩在那儿待上一个钟头，一句话也不说。"},"vary":{"tw":[["change",0],["break",3],["diversify",2],["overlap",6],["alter",0],["move",3],["specific",6],["depart",0]],"en":"At the market the prices vary from week to week, and nobody can say what a box of fruit will cost. My aunt learned to diversify her stall, so that when one thing sold badly, another would carry the day. She would change the signs each morning and alter the way the boxes were stacked. She would also move the heavy ones herself before the first customers came. The rules were the same for all, yet the work never seemed to break her. She said every specific order had to be filled on the day it was made, and a late customer should never depart without something in hand. Nothing about her days overlapped with mine.","zh":"集市上价格一周一周地变，谁也说不准一箱水果要多少钱。我姑学着把摊子做杂一些，这样一样卖不动时，另一样能顶上来。她每天早上改牌子，也改箱子码放的样子。头一批客人来之前，重箱子还是她自己搬。规矩对谁都一样，可这活儿好像从没把她压垮。她说每一张具体的单子都得当天兑上，再晚来的客人也不能空着手走。她的日子和我的几乎不重叠。"},"vote":{"tw":[["ballot",3],["poll",3],["body",2],["party",6],["suffrage",0],["referendum",3],["choice",2],["candidate",6]],"en":"The village hall that year was used for a single vote, and everyone over eighteen came to take part. Each person would mark a ballot behind a low screen and then drop it in a box. A poll had shown that the two sides were almost equal. The old question of suffrage was never raised, because the right had long been given to all. My grandmother said her choice was easy, though she would not name the candidate she backed. In the end the body of neighbours asked for a referendum on the road, and every party had to agree to it.","zh":"那年村礼堂用来办一次投票，十八岁以上的人都来参加。每人躲在矮屏风后面在选票上画一下，再投进箱子里。民调显示两边几乎势均力敌。选举权这个老问题没人再提，因为这份权利早就归了所有人。奶奶说她的选择很容易，可就是不肯说出她支持的那位候选人。最后，邻居们这一群体要求在修路的事上搞一次公投，各方都只好同意。"},"wander":{"tw":[["roll",0],["snake",3],["tell",2],["roam",6],["wind",0],["travel",2],["crawl",6],["cast",0]],"en":"On our last day in the old city we let ourselves wander without a map. A narrow street would wind between two walls, then roll down toward the river. My brother liked to roam ahead and tell me what he saw round each corner. Once a thin snake of water came out of a pipe and crawled across our path. We had travelled a long way to get there, and now we were happy to move slowly. At dusk we sat on a step and cast our eyes back the way we had come. For a while nobody spoke at all.","zh":"在老城的最后一天，我们不拿地图随便走。窄巷在两堵墙间拐来拐去，然后朝河边滑下去。我弟喜欢跑到前头，把每个转角看到的东西讲给我听。有一次一股细水从管子里出来，像蛇一样爬过我们的小路。我们走了很远才到这儿，如今却乐意慢慢走。傍晚我们坐在台阶上，把目光投向来时的方向。好一会儿谁也没说话。"},"worm":{"tw":[["twist",0],["wrench",3],["move",2],["bug",6],["insect",0],["screw",2],["mouse",6],["wrestle",0]],"en":"My grandfather found a worm in the soil while he was turning the beds. It would twist and move as he lifted it, thin as a screw of thread. He said a worm was not a bug and not an insect, but something older than both. A small mouse had been living under the shed, and once he had to wrestle a heavy stone out of the way with a wrench. He would make his own tools and mend them himself. He never threw a living creature out; he put the worm back in the dark soil. He held it between two fingers for a second.","zh":"爷爷翻花畦的时候在土里翻出一条蚯蚓。他把它拎起来，它就扭啊动的，细得像一截螺丝钉上的螺纹。他说蚯蚓既不算虫子也不算昆虫，是比两者都更老的东西。棚子底下住着一只小老鼠，有一回他得用扳手把一块重石头撬开。他自己的工具都自己做、自己修。他从不把活物扔出去，他把蚯蚓放回了黑土里。他在两指间夹了它一小会儿。"},"yell":{"tw":[["call",0],["noise",3],["utter",2],["dare",6],["cry",0],["howl",3],["snore",6],["shout",2]],"en":"That night the baby would not sleep, and my sister was too tired to think. From the next room I heard him yell, then cry, then go quiet. She did not dare to shout, because our father was sleeping and had begun to snore. The only noise in the house was the wind, which seemed to howl under the door. I wanted to call her but I could not utter a word. In the morning she said it was nothing, only a long night, and smiled at me over the table. I made tea and we sat there without talking.","zh":"那天晚上孩子不肯睡，我姐累得脑子都不转了。隔着墙我听见他大叫，接着哭，然后又安静下来。她不敢喊，因为我爸睡着了，还打起了呼噜。屋里唯一的声响是风，在门底下像嚎一样。我想叫她，却一个字也发不出来。早上她说没什么，就是熬了个长夜，隔着桌子冲我笑。我泡了茶，我们就那么坐着没说话。"},"retire":{"tw":[["bed",0],["tire",2],["wait",6],["retreat",0],["travel",2],["quit",6],["withdraw",0]],"en":"My father decided to retire in the spring, after thirty-four years in the same office. He said he was not tired of the work, only tired of the wait for something new. On his last day he did not make a speech; he simply quit the building at four and walked home. His plan was to travel, to withdraw from the noise, and to retreat to a small house near the hills. Now he is in bed by nine and up with the light. He says he has never slept so well.","zh":"我爸决定春天退休，他在同一个办公室待了三十四年。他说他不是干腻了，只是等新东西等腻了。最后一天他没有讲话，四点就收拾东西出了楼，走回家。他的打算是去旅行，从喧闹里退出来，退到山边的一所小房子里。现在他九点就上床，跟着天光起。他说从没睡得这么好。"},"rip":{"tw":[["blood",0],["cut",2],["bleed",6],["pull",0],["attack",2],["plug",6],["rent",0]],"en":"The dog caught the sleeve of my coat and made a long rip from the elbow to the wrist. There was a cut on my arm too, and I could see blood on the cloth. It would bleed for a while, so I pressed a plug of clean cloth over it. I had to pull the coat back on, which opened the rent even wider. The attack had come so fast that I had not even heard it growl. At home my mother sewed the rip and told me to stay away from that gate for a while.","zh":"那条狗咬住了我外套的袖子，从手肘到手腕撕开一道长口子。我胳膊上也有一道划伤，布上能看到血。它会流一会儿，我就拿一团干净的布压住。我还得把外套拉回来，结果那道撕口裂得更大了。它扑上来得太快，我连它低吼都没听见。回到家我妈把口子缝上，叫我这一阵别再靠近那道门。"},"risk":{"tw":[["chance",3],["try",2],["cause",6],["danger",2],["venture",2],["affect",6],["adventure",0]],"en":"The climbers knew the risk before they started, and they still decided to try the north face. A wrong step on the ice could cause more than a broken leg. Their guide said there was no real danger in good weather, but the cold would affect them after dark. It was a venture few people would take. My uncle called it a foolish adventure and told them to turn back. They reached the top at noon and were down by six. Some chances, he said later, are better left untaken. I have never wanted to stand that high again.","zh":"出发前登山的人就知道有危险，可他们还是决定试北面那条坡。在冰上踩错一步，后果不止是摔断一条腿。向导说天气好的话其实没什么真正的危险，但天黑了以后寒气会影响他们。这是很少有人敢做的事。我叔叔说那是愚蠢的冒险，让他们回头。他们中午登顶，六点就下来了。后来他说，有些机会还是别碰为好。我再也不想站到那么高的地方去了。"},"roar":{"tw":[["boom",0],["cry",2],["loud",6],["thunder",3],["laugh",2],["rumble",6],["howl",0]],"en":"That night the storm came down the valley with a roar we could feel in the floor. The thunder was so loud that my little brother began to cry, and then, strangely, to laugh. A low rumble went on under everything, like a second storm far away. Twice the whole sky lit up, and each time the boom seemed closer. Outside, the wind started to howl around the corners of the house. We sat in the kitchen and waited for the morning to come. In the morning the river had risen and the bridge was gone.","zh":"那天夜里，风暴顺着山谷压下来，那阵轰鸣连地板都在颤。雷声大得我弟弟先哭了起来，接着又莫名地笑。一切底下都有一阵低沉的轰响，像远处还有一场风暴。天亮了两次，每一次那炸响都更近。外面，风绕着屋角开始嚎叫。我们坐在厨房里，等天亮。第二天早上河水涨了，桥没了。"},"roof":{"tw":[["cap",0],["dome",3],["control",2],["brick",6],["hood",3],["cover",2],["concrete",6]],"en":"The roof of the old house needed work before winter. My father put on a cap, climbed up, and first lifted the hood of the old car in the yard. He had to control his temper when the wind took the plastic sheet twice. Under the tiles we found brick, concrete, and a small dome of old stone near the chimney. He said we would cover the worst part now and do the rest in spring. The whole job would take two weeks of fine weather. By evening my hands were cut and cold, and the house looked older than ever.","zh":"冬天前，老房子的屋顶得修一修。我爸戴上帽子爬上去，先掀开院子里那辆旧车的引擎盖。风两次把塑料布吹走，他得压住火。瓦片底下我们看到了砖、水泥，还有烟囱边一小块石头砌的圆顶。他说先把最坏的那块盖上，剩下的春天再弄。整个活儿得等两个星期的好天气。到了傍晚我的手又冷又破，房子看着比从前更旧了。"},"schedule":{"tw":[["agenda",0],["book",3],["list",2],["regular",6],["calendar",3],["plan",2],["start",6]],"en":"My schedule that week was full from Monday to Friday, and every item on the agenda seemed urgent. I wrote a list of what had to be done and put it in my book beside the calendar. My plan was to keep to a regular routine: start at eight, stop at six. By Wednesday the whole thing had fallen apart, because two meetings ran long. I had to move three calls to the following week. On Friday I looked at the empty page and felt almost afraid of it. I have never trusted a full page since.","zh":"那一周我的日程从周一排到周五，议程上每一项看着都急。我把必须做的事列了张单子，夹在书里日历旁边。我的打算是保持固定的作息：八点开始，六点收工。到了星期三，整件事就散了架，因为两个会都开超了。我只好把三个电话挪到下一周。星期五我看着那页空白，竟有点怕它。从那以后，我再也不信排得满满的一页了。"},"seal":{"tw":[["stamp",0],["pack",3],["close",2],["remove",6],["varnish",0],["coat",2],["shield",6]],"en":"The letter had to go out that day, so I put a red seal on the back and pressed my stamp into the wax. Then I had to pack the box beside it, close the lid, and remove the old labels from the top. My uncle, who worked with wood, had given the box a coat of varnish the night before, and it still smelled of it. He said a good finish was a kind of shield against the wet. I wrote the address, checked it twice, and carried everything to the door.","zh":"那封信当天就得寄出去，于是我在背面盖了个红印章，把图章压进蜡里。接着我得把旁边的箱子打包，合上盖子，再把旧的标签从上面撕掉。我叔叔是做木工的，前一晚给这箱子刷了一层清漆，现在还闻得到味儿。他说好的漆面能挡潮气，像一层护甲。我写好地址，核对了两遍，把东西拎到门口。"},"select":{"tw":[["choice",0],["field",3],["list",6],["choose",0],["elect",3],["pick",6],["prime",0]],"en":"From a long list of books I had to select five for the course, and the choice was harder than I expected. I walked between the shelves in the field of history and tried to choose by the first page alone. I would pick one up, read a line, and put it back. A friend told me to elect the older titles first, because they had survived the test of time. In the end I took the prime ones and left the rest. Later I wished I had been braver. The books I did not choose are still on that list.","zh":"从一长串书目里我得为这门课挑五本，这选择比我预想的难。我在历史的那片书架间来回走，想只凭第一页来定。拿起一本读一行，又放回去。一个朋友说，先选老一点的书，因为它们经住了时间的考验。最后我拿了最好的那几本，其余的都留下了。后来我有点后悔自己不够大胆。我没选的那些书还在那张单子上。"},"sentence":{"tw":[["condemn",0],["question",3],["term",2],["sentencing",6],["doom",0],["declare",2],["jail",6]],"en":"The judge took a long time before he gave the sentence. He did not condemn the young man without a word of explanation, and he asked one question the lawyers had not expected. The term would be two years, with the sentencing set for the following month. Then he declared that the jail would offer him a chance to learn a trade. I had come to report on the case and found myself writing nothing at all. Outside, the sky was grey and seemed full of doom, but the man looked almost calm.","zh":"法官花了很久才宣判。他没有一句解释就给那个年轻人定罪，还问了一个律师们没料到的问题。刑期是两年，具体量刑定在下个月。接着他宣布，监狱会给他一个学门手艺的机会。我是来报道这案子的，结果一个字也没写。外面天色灰沉，像压着一股厄运，可那个人看上去几乎很平静。"},"shade":{"tw":[["ghost",0],["change",2],["bright",6],["shadow",3],["draw",2],["wet",6],["tone",0]],"en":"In the afternoon we would sit in the shade of the old tree and watch the bright field turn gold. The shadow of its leaves would draw slow shapes on the grass, and the tone of the light would change hour by hour. After the rain the ground stayed wet and cool. My grandmother said the tree was like a ghost of her own childhood, standing in the same place while everything else moved. I did not understand her then. Now I sit in that same shade and think about her. She has been gone for many years, and the tree is still there.","zh":"下午我们常坐在老树的荫里，看明晃晃的田野一点点变成金色。树叶的影子在草地上慢慢画出形状，光线的调子一小时一小时地变。下过雨后地面又湿又凉。奶奶说这棵树像她童年的一个影子，别的东西都挪了地方，它还站在原地。那时我不懂她的话。现在我坐在同一片树荫下，想起她。她已经走了很多年，那棵树还在。"},"shadow":{"tw":[["dark",0],["ghost",3],["follow",2],["image",6],["tail",0],["picture",6],["shade",2]],"en":"My little sister used to follow me everywhere, my shadow for the whole summer. If I went to the shop, she came; if I sat in the shade, she sat beside me. She was afraid of the dark and of every ghost in the stories we told. I once drew her picture on the wall, and she kept pointing at the image and laughing. She held my coat tail all the way home. Years later she still says that summer is the one she remembers best. I was not always patient with her, and I am sorry for that.","zh":"我妹妹以前走到哪儿都跟着我，整个夏天都是我的影子。我去店里她跟去，我坐在荫里她就坐我旁边。她怕黑，也怕我们讲的每个故事里的鬼。有一回我在墙上画了她的样子，她一直指着那个像笑。回家的路上她一路抓着我的衣角。多年以后她还说，那个夏天是她记得最清楚的一个。我对她并不总是有耐心，这一点我很抱歉。"},"shiver":{"tw":[["shake",0],["fear",2],["bleed",6],["chill",0],["reflex",2],["scorch",6],["thrill",0]],"en":"The cold that morning was enough to make anyone shiver, and my hands began to shake before I even reached the gate. I felt a chill that had nothing to do with the weather; it was plain fear. Near the fire the ground was still warm, and I could see where the flames had scorched the fence. A small cut on my knee had started to bleed again. When a dog barked behind me, I jumped before I could think, a pure reflex. Then the lorry came, and with it a strange thrill of relief.","zh":"那天早上冷得谁都会打哆嗦，我还没走到大门口手就开始抖。我感觉到一阵寒意，跟天气无关，就是单纯的害怕。火场附近的地还是温的，能看见火焰把篱笆烧焦的地方。我膝盖上一道小口子又开始流血。身后有条狗叫了一声，我想都没想就跳了起来，纯粹是本能反应。然后卡车来了，随之而来的竟是一阵奇怪的、松了口气的兴奋。"},"shove":{"tw":[["stuff",0],["elbow",3],["push",2],["poke",6],["squeeze",0],["scrape",6],["thrust",0]],"en":"When the bus finally came, everyone began to shove toward the door at once. A man used his elbow to push past me, and a woman with a bag tried to squeeze into the space beside the driver. Someone poked me in the back with a folded umbrella, and my case scraped along the step. I had far too much stuff and no free hand. When the doors opened I was thrust forward by the crowd and had to laugh. In the end we all got on, and the bus was quiet within a minute.","zh":"公共汽车终于来了，所有人一下子都朝门口挤。一个男人用胳膊肘把我推到一边，一个提包的女人想塞进司机旁边的空隙。有人用收起的伞戳我后背，我的箱子在台阶上刮了过去。我东西带得太多，一只手都空不出来。门一开，我被人群顶着往前推，忍不住笑了。最后大家都上了车，不到一分钟车里就静了。"},"sore":{"tw":[["mad",0],["gall",3],["elbow",6],["raw",0],["fester",3],["shoulder",6],["tender",0]],"en":"After the long walk my shoulder was sore for three days. The strap had rubbed the skin raw, and by the second night the gall on it began to fester. I was mad at myself for carrying so much, though there was no one else to blame. My elbow hurt too, but that was from an old fall. The doctor said the place was still tender and told me to rest it. She said not to lift anything heavy for a week, and I did as she said. By Friday I could lift my arm above my head, and the sore spot had almost gone.","zh":"走了那么远的路以后，我的肩膀疼了三天。背带把皮磨破了，到第二天夜里，磨出来的那块伤开始化脓。我气自己带的东西太多，可也怪不得别人。我的手肘也疼，那是以前摔的。医生说那块地方还嫩着，让我别用它，一个星期内不许提重东西。我照做了。到星期五我已经能把胳膊举过头顶，疼的地方也几乎好了。"},"spare":{"tw":[["extra",0],["use",2],["enough",6],["free",0],["score",2],["carry",6],["save",0]],"en":"Before the long drive my father always kept a spare wheel in the back and an extra can of water under the seat. It was not enough to save us from every problem, but it gave him a free mind. He would use the same tools for twenty years and never lose one. That trip began with a score of small troubles: a flat tyre, then a locked door. He carried the spare out himself and changed it in the rain. He said a man should always keep something in reserve. That night we slept by the road and started again at dawn.","zh":"出远门之前，我爸总会在后厢放一个备用轮胎，座位底下再放一罐水。这不足以让我们躲过所有麻烦，但能让他心里踏实。他用同一套工具用了二十年，从没丢过一件。那趟旅行一开始就出了不少小岔子：先是爆胎，接着门又锁死了。他自己把备胎搬出来，在雨里换上。他说人总得给自己留一手。那天夜里我们就睡在路边，天亮才接着走。"},"stiff":{"tw":[["strong",5],["body",2],["soft",6],["tight",0],["man",2],["face",6],["wet",0]],"en":"My neck felt stiff all morning, and my whole body ached from the night before. I had slept on a hard floor, and the air had been cold and wet. A strong man in the next room told me to stand up and move, that sitting still would only make it worse. He had a kind, soft voice, though his face stayed serious. He put a tight band around my arm and counted. Later I learned he had been a nurse. By noon I could turn my head again. The feeling came back slowly, one finger at a time.","zh":"我一上午脖子都是僵的，整个人从头天夜里起就酸痛。我睡在硬地板上，空气又冷又潮。隔壁一个壮实的男人叫我站起来动动，说这么坐着只会更糟。他声音温和，脸上却一直很严肃。他拿一条带子紧紧缠住我的胳膊，数着数。后来我才知道他是护士。到中午我已经能转头了。感觉是一点点回来的，一根手指一根手指地。"},"survive":{"tw":[["last",0],["breathe",3],["succumb",1],["recover",6],["live",0],["find",6],["exist",0]],"en":"After the flood, three families had to survive on what they could find in the ruins. They could not last long without clean water, and one old man seemed ready to succumb to the cold. My aunt helped him breathe again and kept him warm through the night. In the morning he began to recover. They found a dry room and lived there for two weeks while the road was closed. Such places still exist in the hills, where people wait for help that comes slowly. I think about that week more often than I can say.","zh":"洪水过后，有三户人家只能靠从废墟里找到的东西活下来。没有干净的水，他们撑不了多久，有个老人眼看就要被冻垮。我姑妈帮他重新喘上气，整夜让他保持温暖。到了早上他开始好转。他们找到一间干屋子，在那里住了两个星期，直到路通了。山里还有这样的地方，人们等着来得慢的救援。那一周我常常想起，比我能说出来的次数还多。"},"tent":{"tw":[["camp",0],["pavilion",3],["web",2],["makeshift",6],["encamp",0],["shelter",2],["empty",6]],"en":"We put up the tent in a field beside the river, a makeshift shelter of canvas and poles that took an hour to raise. The camp was almost empty that night, and a web of light spread across the sky. In the distance a small wooden pavilion stood at the edge of the trees, where a family had encamped for the summer. We sat and listened to the water. In the morning the mist was so thick that we could not see the far bank, and we were glad of a roof over our heads.","zh":"我们在河边的一块地里搭起了帐篷，那是个用帆布和杆子凑成的临时住处，花了一个小时才立起来。那天夜里营地几乎空着，天上铺开一张光的网。远处树林边有一座小木亭，有一家人整个夏天都扎营在那里。我们坐着听水声。早上雾浓得看不见对岸，我们庆幸头顶好歹有个遮挡。"},"thin":{"tw":[["cut",0],["draw",3],["fat",1],["soft",6],["slight",5],["smooth",6],["lean",0]],"en":"The old man was lean and thin, with a face that seemed cut from wood. He would draw a line on the board, then plane it with slow, smooth strokes until the wood was soft to the touch. He said a slight change in the angle could ruin a whole day of work. There was no fat on his arms, only long muscle, and he never seemed to tire. I watched him for an hour without speaking. He gave me a thin strip of the wood to keep, and I still have it. It has grown dark with age, and it still smells of oil.","zh":"老人又瘦又单薄，一张脸像是用木头削出来的。他会在板上画一道线，然后一下一下慢慢地刨，刨到木头摸着发软。他说角度差一点点，一整天的活儿就毁了。他胳膊上没有肥肉，只有长长的肌肉，好像从不会累。我一声不响看了他一个钟头。他给了我一条薄薄的木片，我到现在还留着。它随着年月变黑了，还带着一股油味。"},"toast":{"tw":[["drink",2],["bread",2],["cake",6],["crisp",0],["heat",2],["butter",6],["pledge",0]],"en":"On Sunday mornings my father would make toast while the rest of us were still in bed. He liked it crisp and dark, with a thick layer of butter, and he would heat the bread until the kitchen smelled of it. My mother had her coffee, my brother had cake, and I had milk to drink. Sometimes he would raise his cup and make a small pledge about the week ahead, and we would all answer. Those mornings were the same for years. I did not know then how much I would miss them.","zh":"星期天早上我们还在睡的时候，我爸就起来做吐司。他喜欢烤得又脆又焦，抹上厚厚一层黄油，把面包烤到整间厨房都是香味。我妈喝咖啡，我弟吃蛋糕，我喝牛奶。有时他会举起杯子，为接下来的一周说几句小小的心愿，我们也都应一声。那样的早晨重复了好多年。那时我不知道自己后来会这么想念。"},"toilet":{"tw":[["pot",0],["head",3],["room",2],["tub",6],["stool",0],["plastic",6],["gutter",0]],"en":"In the little house by the sea the toilet was outside, and at night you had to walk past the gutter to reach it. There was no proper room for washing, only a plastic tub and a stool, and a pot that my grandmother used for the plants. The old sailors in the village still called it the head. I did not mind any of it. The stars were close, and the wind came in off the water. I stood there one night and thought I had never been so far from the city.","zh":"海边那间小屋的厕所在外头，夜里得绕过排水沟才走得过去。没有正经的洗漱间，只有一个塑料盆、一张小凳，还有我奶奶拿来种花的一个罐子。村里的老水手到现在还管它叫船上的厕所。这些我都不在意。星星很近，风从水面上吹来。有一个晚上我站在那儿，觉得自己从没离城市这么远过。"},"tongue":{"tw":[["knife",0],["basque",3],["play",2],["mouth",6],["spit",0],["language",2],["lip",6]],"en":"My grandmother could play with words in three languages, and her tongue could turn a plain sentence into a joke. She said the Basque language was older than the ones spoken around it, though she had never been there. Her mouth would find the right word before anyone else. When she was angry she would bite her lip and say nothing at all. Once she took the knife from my hand, put the blade down, and told me to hold my tongue at the table. Then she would spit out the word I had wanted and laugh.","zh":"我奶奶能用三种语言玩文字游戏，她舌头一动，一句平平常常的话就成了笑话。她说巴斯克语比周围那些语言都古老，虽然她从没去过那里。往往别人还没开口，她嘴里就已经有那个正合适的词了。她生气的时候就咬住嘴唇，一个字也不说。有一次她从我手里拿过刀，把刀刃放下，叫我在饭桌上闭嘴。然后她会把我想要的那个词吐出来，笑我。"},"tough":{"tw":[["bad",5],["criminal",2],["tender",1],["face",6],["hard",5],["easy",6],["bully",3]],"en":"The new boy had a hard face and a name that people said meant trouble. Two older students, a bully and a small criminal in the making, decided to make his first week tough. The test on Friday was bad enough, but their jokes were worse. He did not cry or run. He simply stood there, calm and almost tender when he spoke to the younger ones. By Monday they had given up. It is easy to be hard, he told me later; it is much harder to stay kind. I have remembered that sentence for thirty years.","zh":"新来的那个男生有张硬邦邦的脸，据说他的名字就带着麻烦。两个高年级的学生——一个横的，一个眼看着要学坏——决心让他头一个星期难过。星期五的考试已经够糟，他们的玩笑更糟。他没哭也没跑。他只是站在那儿，跟年纪小的说话时语气平静得近乎温和。到了星期一，他们就放弃了。后来他跟我说，装狠容易，一直对人好才难。那句话我记了三十年。"},"trick":{"tw":[["joke",0],["shift",2],["game",6],["fox",0],["device",2],["ball",6],["magic",0]],"en":"The old man on the corner could do one card trick that nobody could work out. He would ask you to pick a card, shift the pack, and then show it to you as if by magic. It was not a cruel joke, only a small game he played with strangers. He said the secret was in the wrist, not in any clever device. A fox of a man, my father called him, meaning it kindly. Once he made a ball of paper disappear, and a boy of six ran home still laughing. He never asked anyone for money.","zh":"街角那个老人有一个纸牌戏法，谁也看不透。他会让你挑一张牌，把牌堆一错，然后像变魔术一样把它亮出来。那不是什么损人的玩笑，只是他跟陌生人玩的一个小游戏。他说窍门在手腕上，不在什么巧妙的机关。我爸管他叫老狐狸，是句好话。有一回他把一个纸团变没了，一个六岁的孩子笑着跑回了家。他从不跟人要钱。"},"twin":{"tw":[["couple",0],["grow",2],["jet",6],["pair",0],["join",2],["crash",6],["match",2]],"en":"My twin sister and I were born ten minutes apart, and people still cannot match our faces to our names. We grew up in the same room, a quiet pair who said little to anyone else. As children we had a small jet plane and a wooden couple of dolls that we would join at the hands. Then, in our twenties, we had a bad crash in the mountains, and one of us broke an arm. Only our family could tell which. We have lived apart for years now, but the two of us still answer at the same time.","zh":"我和我双胞胎姐姐出生时差了十分钟，到现在别人还是对不上我们的脸和名字。我们在同一个房间长大，是一对不怎么跟外人说话的人。小时候我们有一架小喷气机和一对木头娃娃，总把它们的手拉到一起。后来二十多岁那年，我们在山里出了场严重的车祸，我们中一个摔断了胳膊。只有家里人分得清是哪一个。如今我们分开住了好些年，可两个人还是会同时开口回答。"},"warn":{"tw":[["admonish",0],["alarm",3],["inform",2],["worry",6],["caution",3],["order",2],["fear",6]],"en":"The radio began to warn us about the river at four in the morning. The voice did not shout; it simply informed us that the water was rising and told us to move to higher ground. I did not want to worry my mother, who was still asleep. It was my job to caution the old people, who did not want to leave. My father tried to admonish me for going out, but I had no time to listen. I could feel the fear in my own hands. When the alarm rang again, we left, and later I learned that the order had saved two streets.","zh":"凌晨四点，收音机开始播报河水的警报。那个声音没有喊，只是通知我们水位在涨，让我们往高处撤。我不想吵醒我妈，她还在睡。我的任务是去劝那些不肯走的老人。我爸想训我，说我不该往外跑，可我哪有空听。我能感觉到自己的手在抖。警报再响的时候，我们走了，后来我才知道，那道命令救了两条街。"}}});
